-- ¶3: the day of signing.
@ref akn:preamble/p3
`the 2016 framework agreement was signed on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 18 4 2016

-- ¶29: the parties negotiated the cost frame of the wage agreements for
-- the employers' employees for 1.1.2013–31.12.2017, and further benefits
-- for that time.
@ref akn:preamble/p29
`the 2016 framework's period of the cost frame opens on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2013

§§ `1–3 מבוא, תקופה ותחולה`

-- akn:art_1 The heading of §1.
-- akn:art_2 The heading of §2.
-- akn:art_3 The heading of §3.

-- §1 ¶1: the preamble is part of the agreement. ¶2: its headings are for
-- convenience only and do not bear on its reading — the agreement itself
-- answering what convention precedence.heading answers where a text is
-- silent. ¶3: naming a provision of the Takshir does not change its
-- normative standing.
@ref akn:art_1/p1
`the 2016 framework agreement's preamble is part of it` MEANS TRUE

@ref akn:art_1/p2
`the 2016 framework agreement's headings bear on its reading` MEANS FALSE

@ref akn:art_1/p3
`naming the Takshir in the 2016 framework changes its standing` MEANS FALSE

-- §2: the agreement is for the time to 31.12.2017 ("תקופת ההסכם"), the day
-- in (convention dates.end).
@ref akn:art_2/p1
`the 2016 framework agreement's period ends on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2017

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in the 2016 framework agreement's period` d IF
    d `is on or before` `the 2016 framework agreement's period ends on`

-- §3(א) ¶1: it covers every employee of an employer that signed it whose
-- pay is computed by the collective agreements of a scale the Histadrut
-- represents that annex א' lists ("עובד"), as the agreement and the
-- agreements of §11 set out. Annex א' keeps out of the jurists', the public
-- defenders' and the state attorneys' scales those whose pay is linked to a
-- judicial officer's.
@desc An employee, as far as the framework agreement of 18.4.2016 asks.
DECLARE `2016 framework employee` HAS
    `employed by an employer that signed the 2016 framework agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the scale his pay is computed by under the 2016 framework` IS A STRING @desc the scale's name as annex א' prints it
    `his pay is linked to a judicial officer's under the 2016 framework` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref akn:art_3__para_a
GIVEN e IS A `2016 framework employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2016 framework agreement covers` e IF
        e's `employed by an employer that signed the 2016 framework agreement`
    AND elem (e's `the scale his pay is computed by under the 2016 framework`) `the scales annex א' of the 2016 framework lists`
    AND NOT (    e's `his pay is linked to a judicial officer's under the 2016 framework`
             AND elem (e's `the scale his pay is computed by under the 2016 framework`) `the annex א' scales of 2016 that leave out one linked to a judicial officer`)

-- (א) ¶2: the payments that allocate the cost frame, under this agreement
-- and the agreements of §11, go to an employee employed in the months they
-- are paid.
@ref akn:art_3__para_a/p2
GIVEN `employed in the month of the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an allocation payment of the 2016 framework goes to the employee` `employed in the month of the payment` IF
    `employed in the month of the payment`

-- (א) ¶3: §19 (budgetary pensioners) reaches whom it says. ¶4: §18 (parents'
-- hours at the end of August) reaches too one whose pay is linked to a
-- judicial officer's and who is in the jurists' scale.
@ref akn:art_3__para_a/p3 akn:art_3__para_a/p4
GIVEN `the section` IS A NUMBER, e IS A `2016 framework employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section of the 2016 framework reaches` `the section` e IF
        `the 2016 framework agreement covers` e
    OR (    `the section` EQUALS 18
        AND e's `employed by an employer that signed the 2016 framework agreement`
        AND e's `his pay is linked to a judicial officer's under the 2016 framework`
        AND e's `the scale his pay is computed by under the 2016 framework` EQUALS "משפטנים")

-- (ב): for the scales ¶2 lists, the cost frame is allocated by separate
-- collective agreements signed alongside this one, so — to prevent double
-- payment — §§4, 5.1, 6 to 8, 10 to 15 and 19 to 21 do not apply to them
-- unless those agreements say otherwise. ¶2: students; physiotherapists;
-- occupational therapists; paramedical staff; radiographers; laboratory
-- workers, chemists and microbiologists; pharmacists; social workers
-- employed by the Ministry of Health, Clalit, Hadassah or the two cities'
-- hospitals; and a psychologist in the academics' or psychologists' scale
-- (in a field of §2 of the agreement of 25.3.2001, or educational, social
-- and occupational or medical, or an intern of its §2.4).
@ref akn:art_3__para_b akn:art_3__para_b/p2
`the sections §3(ב) keeps from the separately allocated scales` MEANS
    LIST 4, 5.1, 6, 7, 8, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15, 19, 20, 21

`the scales §3(ב) of the 2016 framework allocates separately` MEANS
    LIST "סטודנטים", "פיזיותרפיסטים", "מרפאים בעיסוק", "פארא-רפואיים", "רנטגנאים",
         "עובדי מעבדות, כימאים ומיקרוביולוגים", "רוקחים", "עובדים סוציאליים במשרד הבריאות, בכללית, בהדסה או בבתי החולים הממשלתיים-עירוניים", "פסיכולוג"

GIVEN `the section` IS A NUMBER, `in a scale of §3(ב)` IS A BOOLEAN, `its separate agreement says otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section of the 2016 framework applies beside §3(ב)` `the section` `in a scale of §3(ב)` `its separate agreement says otherwise` IF
        NOT `in a scale of §3(ב)`
    OR `its separate agreement says otherwise`
    OR NOT elem `the section` `the sections §3(ב) keeps from the separately allocated scales`

-- (ג): it covers too an employee whose pay is by the Histadrut's agreements
-- and who is employed by another employer that signs the accession letter
-- of annex ב', as it says; joining with changes needs the chair of the
-- trade union division's approval and, for a budgeted or supported body
-- under the Budget Foundations Law, the wages commissioner's too.
@ref akn:art_3__para_c
GIVEN `the employer signed the accession letter as annex ב' prints it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `joined with changes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trade union division's chair approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a budgeted or supported body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the wages commissioner approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an employer has joined the 2016 framework` `the employer signed the accession letter as annex ב' prints it` `joined with changes` `the trade union division's chair approved` `a budgeted or supported body` `the wages commissioner approved` IF
        `the employer signed the accession letter as annex ב' prints it`
    AND (   NOT `joined with changes`
         OR (    `the trade union division's chair approved`
             AND ((NOT `a budgeted or supported body`) OR `the wages commissioner approved`)))

§§ `4–5 מסגרת עלות התוספות, הקצאתה והמענק`

-- akn:art_4 The heading of §4.
-- akn:art_5 The heading of §5.
-- akn:art_4/p1 The heading of §4's first part: in the State's service and among the other employers.

-- §4 ¶2–¶3: the cost frame of the wage supplements and the money benefits
-- for 1.1.2013–31.12.2017, in the State's service and among the other
-- employers that signed, is 7.5%: 1.5% for each of 2013, 2014, 2015, 2016
-- and 2017. ¶4: it is allocated by the dates and spread of §5.
@ref akn:art_4/p2 akn:art_4/p3 akn:art_4/p4
`the 2016 framework cost frame in all` MEANS 7.5%
`the 2016 framework cost frame for each year` MEANS 1.5%
`the years of the 2016 framework cost frame` MEANS LIST 2013, 2014, 2015, 2016, 2017

#ASSERT sum (map (GIVEN y YIELD `the 2016 framework cost frame for each year`) `the years of the 2016 framework cost frame`) EQUALS `the 2016 framework cost frame in all`

-- 5.1: the frame is allocated at five dates, each on the salary base of
-- §6.1 (and ¶2, as §6 sets the base): 5.1.1 from 1.7.2016, 1% (its manner
-- §10's); 5.1.2 from 1.3.2017, completed to 2.75%; 5.1.3 from 1.1.2018, to
-- 4.25%; 5.1.4 from 1.6.2018, to 6%; 5.1.5 from 1.12.2018, to 7.5%.
-- "השלמה ל-" makes the figure the whole allocation from its day
-- (convention dates.start for each day).
@desc A step of the 2016 framework's allocation: from its day, the whole allocation is its figure.
DECLARE `2016 framework step` HAS
    `the step's clause` IS A STRING
    `the step's day`    IS A DATE
    `completed to`      IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:art_5__para_5-1 akn:art_5__para_5-1__subpara_5-1-1 akn:art_5__para_5-1__subpara_5-1-1/p2 akn:art_5__para_5-1__subpara_5-1-2 akn:art_5__para_5-1__subpara_5-1-3 akn:art_5__para_5-1__subpara_5-1-4 akn:art_5__para_5-1__subpara_5-1-5 akn:art_5__para_5-1/p2
`the steps of the 2016 framework` MEANS
    LIST `2016 framework step` "5.1.1" (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2016) (1%),
         `2016 framework step` "5.1.2" (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2017) (2.75%),
         `2016 framework step` "5.1.3" (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2018) (4.25%),
         `2016 framework step` "5.1.4" (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2018) (6%),
         `2016 framework step` "5.1.5" (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2018) (7.5%)

-- The allocation on a day: the figure of the last step begun by it.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2016 framework allocation on` d IS
    foldl (GIVEN acc, s YIELD IF d `is on or after` (s's `the step's day`) THEN s's `completed to` ELSE acc) 0 `the steps of the 2016 framework`

-- What a step adds to the step before it.
GIVEN s IS A `2016 framework step`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `what a 2016 framework step adds` s IS
    s's `completed to` MINUS `the 2016 framework allocation on` (DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL (s's `the step's day`) MINUS 1))

#ASSERT `the 2016 framework allocation on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2016) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the 2016 framework allocation on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2018) EQUALS `the 2016 framework cost frame in all`
#ASSERT map `what a 2016 framework step adds` `the steps of the 2016 framework` EQUALS LIST 1%, 1.75%, 1.5%, 1.75%, 1.5%

-- 5.2: a one-time grant as well, 2,000 in all, in two parts of 1,000.
-- 5.2.1: the first part was paid by the wages commissioner's circulars הע
-- 2016-1-3 (14.1.2016, "the grant circular") and 2016-1-12 (11.2.2016),
-- annex ג' ("the grant circulars"); ¶2: the other employers that signed
-- have applied or will apply them, as the wages commissioner's approval in
-- the grant circular sets out, and one that has not yet paid pays it with
-- the salary of the month after it signed, at the latest the month after.
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-2 akn:art_5__para_5-2/p2 akn:art_5__para_5-2__subpara_5-2-1 akn:art_5__para_5-2__subpara_5-2-1/p2
`the 2016 framework's one-time grant in all` MEANS 2000
`a part of the 2016 framework's one-time grant` MEANS 1000

#ASSERT 2 TIMES `a part of the 2016 framework's one-time grant` EQUALS `the 2016 framework's one-time grant in all`

GIVEN `the month the employer signed` IS A NUMBER @desc counted as year × 12 + month
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the latest salary month another employer pays the grant's first part in` `the month the employer signed` IS
    `the month the employer signed` PLUS 2

-- 5.2.2: the second part is paid with the January 2017 salary (paid in
-- February 2017), at the latest with February's, to those entitled to the
-- first part; ¶2: it equals the first part paid to the employee.
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-2__subpara_5-2-2 akn:art_5__para_5-2__subpara_5-2-2/p2
GIVEN `the first part he was paid` IS A NUMBER, `entitled to the first part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the grant's second part` `the first part he was paid` `entitled to the first part` IS
    IF `entitled to the first part` THEN `the first part he was paid` ELSE 0

`the grant's second part is paid with the salary for` MEANS LIST 2017, 1
`the grant's second part is paid at the latest with the salary for` MEANS LIST 2017, 2

-- 5.2.3: the grant circular's 1(ו)(9) is amended: (1) 29.12.2016 in place
-- of 31.1.2017 — the end of the time in which an employee on unpaid leave
-- must have four months and a day of salary in a row; (2) the grant to such
-- an employee is paid with the January 2017 salary, at the latest with
-- February's. The circular as it stands in annex ג' prints the earlier
-- figures (encoded there); these are the rule from the signing.
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-2__subpara_5-2-3 akn:art_5__para_5-2__subpara_5-2-3__cls_5-2-3-1 akn:art_5__para_5-2__subpara_5-2-3__cls_5-2-3-2
`the last day of the unpaid-leave test, as 5.2.3 amends it` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 29 12 2016
`the salary month an unpaid-leave grant is paid with, as 5.2.3 amends it` MEANS LIST 2017, 1
`the latest salary month an unpaid-leave grant is paid with, as 5.2.3 amends it` MEANS LIST 2017, 2

-- The special dates under 5.2.3 (its second heading): (א) one whose first
-- part is paid with the January 2017 salary under 1(ו)(9)(3) is paid the
-- second with it, the same sum; (ב) one who, when the second part is paid,
-- is (1) on sick leave without pay, (2) on maternity leave, or (3) absent
-- for an injury at work not charged to his sick leave (Takshir 33.6), is
-- paid it with the first salary on his return, at the latest the month
-- after; (ג) one whose employment ends before it is paid has it with his
-- last salary.
-- not weighed against `the Sick Pay Law`: the agreement names sick leave
-- only as an absence that keeps a grant's run or puts off its payment to
-- the return to work (§5.2.3(ב)(1), and the annexed circulars 2016-1-3,
-- §1(ו)(6)–(7), and 2016-1-12, §3), and as
-- leave that is not a parent's leave day (§18.1.2); the law sets sick pay
-- and the days that accrue for it, and nothing on a grant or on other
-- leave, so none of these rules on what the law puts a floor under.

-- not weighed against `the Annual Leave Law`: the agreement names annual
-- leave only as a condition of the parents' special hours (§18.1.2, no
-- more than 22 or 26 days of it a year, every kind counted; §18.1.3, no
-- other leave benefit in July and August). The hours come on top of the
-- leave and take no day of it, and the law says nothing on who has a
-- benefit beyond it, so the clause rules nothing the law puts a floor
-- under.

-- not weighed against `the Advance Notice Law`: annex 8 names "the
-- dismissal procedure in the State service" only as the subject of a
-- labour dispute it lists; it gives or asks no notice, so it rules nothing
-- the law puts a floor under.

DECLARE `2016 grant absence` IS ONE OF
    `on sick leave without pay when the 2016 grant is paid`
    `on maternity leave when the 2016 grant is paid`
    `absent for an injury at work when the 2016 grant is paid`
    `at work when the 2016 grant is paid`

@ref akn:art_5__para_5-2__subpara_5-2-3__hc_1 akn:art_5__para_5-2__subpara_5-2-3__hc_1__cls_a akn:art_5__para_5-2__subpara_5-2-3__hc_1__cls_b akn:art_5__para_5-2__subpara_5-2-3__hc_1__cls_b__pnt_a akn:art_5__para_5-2__subpara_5-2-3__hc_1__cls_b__pnt_b akn:art_5__para_5-2__subpara_5-2-3__hc_1__cls_b__pnt_c akn:art_5__para_5-2__subpara_5-2-3__hc_1__cls_c
GIVEN `his first part is paid with the January 2017 salary` IS A BOOLEAN
      absence IS A `2016 grant absence`
      `employment ends before the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `when the grant's second part is paid` `his first part is paid with the January 2017 salary` absence `employment ends before the payment` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `employment ends before the payment` THEN "with his last salary"
        IF `his first part is paid with the January 2017 salary` THEN "with the first part, in the January 2017 salary"
        IF NOT absence EQUALS `at work when the 2016 grant is paid` THEN "with the first salary on his return, at the latest the month after"
        OTHERWISE "with the January 2017 salary, at the latest February's"

-- 5.2.4: the State may, at its discretion, pay the second part earlier;
-- that does not bind the other employers to pay early.
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-2__subpara_5-2-4
`the State may pay the grant's second part early` MEANS TRUE
`the State paying early binds the other employers` MEANS FALSE

§§ `6–8 הבסיס, החישוב ושכר המינימום`

-- akn:art_6 The heading of §6.
-- akn:art_7 The heading of §7.
-- akn:art_8 The heading of §8.

-- 6.1: the salary base of §5.1 is the monthly average over January–December
-- 2015 of the combined salary, seniority, every cost-of-living increment
-- paid to 31.12.2015, and the wage supplements and supplements to pay
-- (shekel and percentage, "התוספות"), save (1) those not paid monthly,
-- weekly or daily, and (2) those not updated by the cost-of-living
-- agreements that have another updating mechanism — where ¶2 makes a
-- supplement set to grow at the framework's rates no "other mechanism": it
-- is in the base, and counting it there is its update, with no double.
-- 6.2: in for the avoidance of doubt: (1) overtime, shifts, duty rosters,
-- on-call, call-outs and incentive pay; (2) supplements, annual
-- supplements and annual grants derived from the hour-value salary, the
-- combined salary or the budgetary pension's determining salary; (3) the
-- minimum-wage top-up. 6.3: expense reimbursements are out. 6.4: only what
-- was paid in January–December 2015; a component first paid after
-- December 2015 is out unless agreed.
@desc A pay component, as §§6 and 9 of the 2016 framework ask about it.
DECLARE `2016 framework pay component` HAS
    `paid monthly, weekly or daily`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `updated by the cost-of-living agreements`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `set to grow at the framework's rates`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `an expense reimbursement`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `paid in 2015`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `first paid after December 2015`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `agreed into the base`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `counted for the hour value`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `bound to the hour value or the pension salary` IS A BOOLEAN
    `one of 6.2's three`                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc overtime and the like, supplements derived from the base salaries, or the minimum-wage top-up

@ref akn:art_6__para_6-1 akn:art_6__para_6-1/p2 akn:art_6__para_6-1__subpara_1 akn:art_6__para_6-1__subpara_2 akn:art_6__para_6-1__subpara_2/p2 akn:art_6__para_6-2 akn:art_6__para_6-2__subpara_1 akn:art_6__para_6-2__subpara_2 akn:art_6__para_6-2__subpara_3 akn:art_6__para_6-3 akn:art_6__para_6-4
GIVEN c IS A `2016 framework pay component`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in the base of the 2016 framework cost frame` c IF
        NOT c's `an expense reimbursement`
    AND (c's `paid in 2015` OR (c's `first paid after December 2015` AND c's `agreed into the base`))
    AND (   c's `one of 6.2's three`
         OR (    c's `paid monthly, weekly or daily`
             AND (c's `updated by the cost-of-living agreements` OR c's `set to grow at the framework's rates`)))

GIVEN `the twelve months of 2015` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2016 framework salary base from` `the twelve months of 2015` IS
    sum `the twelve months of 2015` DIVIDED BY 12

-- 6.5: a claim by the Histadrut that a supplement of 6.1(1) or (2) belongs
-- in the base goes to the follow-up committee of §27.
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-5
`a claim on the 2016 base's exceptions goes to the follow-up committee` MEANS TRUE

-- §7 ¶1: the cost is computed as follows. 7.1: for each scale apart, and
-- for each scale together across every employer that signed and has it,
-- save Israel Post and the Jewish Agency. 7.2: notwithstanding: (א) the
-- firefighters' and the uniform scale in the national fire authority
-- together; (ב) the administrative scale of the State, the NII and the
-- Employment Service with the uniform scale of the two cities' hospitals
-- and Hadassah; (ג) the special scales of the State (the land authority,
-- the border crossings, the judges' typists, Yahalom) together, by annex
-- ד'; (ד)–(ה) the engineers, and the technicians and practical engineers,
-- as (ח)(1)–(5) say for each, each apart from every other scale; (ו) the
-- academic technical scale (מקצ"ט): the institutions of higher education
-- together, the State apart; (ז) the uniform scale: (1) the institutions
-- of higher education together, (2) every local authority together, the
-- regional councils and the three cities included, (3) every religious
-- council together, (4) Clalit apart — ¶2: save those of (א) or (ב); (ח)
-- the academics (auditors included) and journalists together, the
-- psychologists out (they have their own agreement): (1) the State, the
-- NII, the Employment Service, Hadassah and the two cities' hospitals
-- together; (2) the institutions of higher education; (3) the local
-- authorities, save the academics of the cities' hospitals; (4) the
-- religious councils, with the neighbourhood and settlement rabbis; (5)
-- Clalit apart; (ט) the local authorities' uniform and academic scales
-- (§20.1) as §20 says, for 5.1.1's cost; (י) the neighbourhood and
-- settlement rabbis: with the religious councils' academics, or every
-- local authority together. 7.3: Israel Post, all its scales together.
-- 7.4: the Jewish Agency, the WZO, the JNF and Keren Hayesod, each scale
-- and each body apart. 7.5: "the State" includes the defence plants for
-- the Histadrut's employees of the same scale. 7.6: the scales and
-- employers computed together are "the calculation group". The groups are
-- data the agreement describes; the encoding keeps the group as an input
-- (a name) and states the rules that bind it.
@ref akn:art_7/p1 akn:art_7__para_7-1 akn:art_7__para_7-2 akn:art_7__para_7-2__subpara_a akn:art_7__para_7-2__subpara_b akn:art_7__para_7-2__subpara_c akn:art_7__para_7-2__subpara_d akn:art_7__para_7-2__subpara_e akn:art_7__para_7-2__subpara_f akn:art_7__para_7-2__subpara_f__cls_1 akn:art_7__para_7-2__subpara_f__cls_2 akn:art_7__para_7-2__subpara_g akn:art_7__para_7-2__subpara_g__cls_1 akn:art_7__para_7-2__subpara_g__cls_2 akn:art_7__para_7-2__subpara_g__cls_3 akn:art_7__para_7-2__subpara_g__cls_4 akn:art_7__para_7-2__subpara_g/p2 akn:art_7__para_7-2__subpara_h akn:art_7__para_7-2__subpara_h__cls_1 akn:art_7__para_7-2__subpara_h__cls_2 akn:art_7__para_7-2__subpara_h__cls_3 akn:art_7__para_7-2__subpara_h__cls_4 akn:art_7__para_7-2__subpara_h__cls_5 akn:art_7__para_7-2__subpara_i akn:art_7__para_7-2__subpara_j akn:art_7__para_7-3 akn:art_7__para_7-4 akn:art_7__para_7-5 akn:art_7__para_7-6
@desc A calculation group of §7.6: the scales and employers whose cost is computed together.
DECLARE `2016 calculation group` HAS
    `the group's name`                      IS A STRING
    `the group's scales`                    IS A LIST OF STRING
    `the group's employers`                 IS A LIST OF STRING

`the employers §7.1 computes apart` MEANS LIST "חברת דואר ישראל בע\"מ", "הסוכנות היהודית"
`the special scales of the State's service` MEANS LIST "רשות מקרקעי ישראל", "מעברי הגבול", "קלדניות שופטים", "יהלום"
`the psychologists are in the academics' group under §7.2(ח)` MEANS FALSE
`the defence plants are the State for §7` MEANS TRUE

-- 7.2(ח)(1), for example: the academics of the State, the NII, the
-- Employment Service, Hadassah and the two cities' hospitals.
`the State's academics' group of 2016` MEANS
    `2016 calculation group` WITH
        `the group's name`      IS "מח\"ר — המדינה, ביטוח לאומי, שירות התעסוקה, הדסה ובתי החולים הממשלתיים-עירוניים"
        `the group's scales`    IS LIST "מח\"ר", "עיתונאים"
        `the group's employers` IS LIST "המדינה", "המוסד לביטוח לאומי", "שירות התעסוקה", "הסתדרות מדיצינית הדסה", "עיריית תל-אביב יפו", "עיריית חיפה"

-- 7.7: the Histadrut may notify the employers by 30.4.2016 of a change in
-- a calculation group (its scales or employers), in writing to every
-- employer concerned and to the wages commissioner; not for the special
-- scales of the State, where §11.5 governs.
@ref akn:art_7__para_7-7
`the last day to notify a change in a calculation group` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 30 4 2016

GIVEN `notified on` IS A DATE, `in writing to every employer and the wages commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN, `a special scale of the State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a change in a calculation group stands` `notified on` `in writing to every employer and the wages commissioner` `a special scale of the State` IF
        `notified on` `is on or before` `the last day to notify a change in a calculation group`
    AND `in writing to every employer and the wages commissioner`
    AND NOT `a special scale of the State`

-- §8 ¶1: the supplements agreed in the frame do not count toward the
-- minimum-wage top-up under the Minimum Wage Law, and are an "excluded
-- supplement" for its temporary provision of 2015. ¶2: where an existing
-- supplement that does count is raised, ¶1 does not reach it — but that
-- takes nothing from the frame, and the cost saved by it must still be
-- allocated.
@ref akn:art_8/p1 akn:art_8/p2
GIVEN `raises an existing supplement counted for the minimum wage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a 2016 framework supplement counts for the minimum-wage top-up` `raises an existing supplement counted for the minimum wage` IF
    `raises an existing supplement counted for the minimum wage`

`allocating the cost a minimum-wage supplement saves` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `allocate the cost saved by raising a supplement counted for the minimum wage`

`why the Minimum Wage Law is not in the 2016 framework` MEANS
    `outside the corpus` "חוק שכר מינימום, התשמ\"ז-1987, והוראת השעה של התשע\"ה-2015"

§§ `9 הגדלת תוספות מיוחדות`

-- akn:art_9 The heading of §9.

-- 9.1: the wage supplements that, all three, (1) are not counted for the
-- hour value, (2) are none of 12.1(ב)'s (1)–(3), and (3) are not affected
-- by the hour value nor updated with the pension's determining salary, are
-- updated as 9.2 says ("special supplements"); ¶2: not an expense
-- reimbursement of any kind. 12.1(ב)'s three: not paid monthly, weekly or
-- daily; not updated by the cost-of-living agreements, with another
-- mechanism; the minimum-wage top-up.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-1 akn:art_9__para_9-1__subpara_1 akn:art_9__para_9-1__subpara_2 akn:art_9__para_9-1__subpara_3 akn:art_9__para_9-1/p2
GIVEN c IS A `2016 framework pay component`, `the minimum-wage top-up` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a special supplement of the 2016 framework` c `the minimum-wage top-up` IF
        NOT c's `counted for the hour value`
    AND c's `paid monthly, weekly or daily`
    AND c's `updated by the cost-of-living agreements`
    AND NOT `the minimum-wage top-up`
    AND NOT c's `bound to the hour value or the pension salary`
    AND NOT c's `an expense reimbursement`

-- 9.2: each special supplement is updated on the frame's own days and to
-- its own figures — 1% from 1.7.2016, completed to 2.75% from 1.3.2017, to
-- 4.25% from 1.1.2018, to 6% from 1.6.2018 and to 7.5% from 1.12.2018 — of
-- "the base sum": the supplement paid on the eve of the signing under the
-- wages commissioner's circulars (¶1–¶2). The rise is relative (convention
-- amounts.increase).
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-2 akn:art_9__para_9-2__subpara_9-2-1 akn:art_9__para_9-2__subpara_9-2-2 akn:art_9__para_9-2__subpara_9-2-3 akn:art_9__para_9-2__subpara_9-2-4 akn:art_9__para_9-2__subpara_9-2-5 akn:art_9/p1 akn:art_9/p2
GIVEN d IS A DATE, `the base sum` IS A NUMBER @desc the supplement paid on the eve of 18.4.2016 under the wages commissioner's circulars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a special supplement of 2016 on` d `the base sum` IS
    `the base sum` `increased by` (`the 2016 framework allocation on` d)

#ASSERT `a special supplement of 2016 on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2018) 1000 EQUALS 1075

§§ `10 תוספת שקלית 2016`

-- akn:art_10 The heading of §10.

-- 10.1: from 1.7.2016 the employees have a new monthly shekel supplement,
-- the same sum for every full-position employee of the calculation group
-- ("תוספת שקלית 2016"). 10.2: its sum is the one that makes A + B = C:
-- A, its aggregate had it been paid in 2015 to the whole group by 2015's
-- data (part-time and part-year included) and 10.3–10.9; B, the aggregate
-- by which 6.2(1) and (2)'s components paid in 2015 would have grown with
-- it; C, 1% of §6's base for the group, the special supplements of §9
-- left out. ¶3: one sum alone satisfies it. A and B are each the sum times
-- a figure of the group's 2015 data (its full-position months, and the
-- growth of 6.2(1)–(2) per shekel of it): inputs. The sum is C over their
-- total; both positive, it is one.
@ref akn:art_10__para_10-1 akn:art_10__para_10-2 akn:art_10__para_10-2/p2 akn:art_10__para_10-2/p3 akn:art_10__para_10-2/p4 akn:art_10__para_10-2/p5 akn:art_10__para_10-2/p6 akn:art_10__para_10-2/p7
`the 2016 shekel supplement starts on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2016
`the share of the base C takes for the 2016 shekel supplement` MEANS 1%

GIVEN `the group's base without the special supplements` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `C of the 2016 shekel supplement` `the group's base without the special supplements` IS
    `the share of the base C takes for the 2016 shekel supplement` TIMES `the group's base without the special supplements`

GIVEN C IS A NUMBER
      `the group's full-position months in 2015` IS A NUMBER @desc A per shekel of the supplement
      `the growth of 6.2(1)–(2) per shekel` IS A NUMBER @desc B per shekel of the supplement
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the shekel sum that makes A + B = C` C `the group's full-position months in 2015` `the growth of 6.2(1)–(2) per shekel` IS
    C DIVIDED BY (`the group's full-position months in 2015` PLUS `the growth of 6.2(1)–(2) per shekel`)

`an example group's 2016 shekel supplement` MEANS
    `the shekel sum that makes A + B = C` (`C of the 2016 shekel supplement` 12000000) 1500 100

`the example's A + B` MEANS
    `an example group's 2016 shekel supplement` TIMES 1500 PLUS `an example group's 2016 shekel supplement` TIMES 100

#ASSERT `the example's A + B` EQUALS `C of the 2016 shekel supplement` 12000000

-- 10.3: a part-time employee has it in proportion to his position.
@ref akn:art_10__para_10-3
GIVEN `the full-position sum` IS A NUMBER, position IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2016 shekel supplement for a position of` `the full-position sum` position IS
    `the full-position sum` `pro rata to a position of` position

-- 10.4: each group's sum needs the wages commissioner's express written
-- approval, among other things to make sure it does not pass C; so too
-- every rise of it under this agreement.
@ref akn:art_10__para_10-4
GIVEN `the sum` IS A NUMBER, `the full-position months` IS A NUMBER, `the growth per shekel` IS A NUMBER, C IS A NUMBER, `approved in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a 2016 shekel sum may be paid` `the sum` `the full-position months` `the growth per shekel` C `approved in writing` IF
        `approved in writing`
    AND `the sum` TIMES (`the full-position months` PLUS `the growth per shekel`) AT MOST C

`approving the 2016 shekel sum` MEANS
    PARTY `the wages commissioner`
    MUST  `approve the 2016 shekel supplement's amount in writing`

-- 10.5: from January 2017 the sum is updated once a year, in January, by
-- the rise of the new index (December of the year before the update) over
-- the previous one (December of the year before the previous update; for
-- the first, December 2015, published in January 2016) — the consumer
-- price index of the Central Bureau of Statistics. A fall makes no update;
-- the update waits until it can be made upward, the fall offset in full,
-- against the last index used. So the index in force is the highest
-- December index from 2015 to the December before the update.
@ref akn:art_10__para_10-5 akn:art_10__para_10-5/p2 akn:art_10__para_10-5/p3 akn:art_10__para_10-5/p4 akn:art_10__para_10-5/p5 akn:art_10__para_10-5/p6
GIVEN `the sum` IS A NUMBER
      `December 2015's index` IS A NUMBER
      `the December indices since` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc December 2016 to the December before the update, in order
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2016 shekel supplement updated by the index` `the sum` `December 2015's index` `the December indices since` IS
    `the sum` TIMES (foldl (GIVEN m, i YIELD IF i GREATER THAN m THEN i ELSE m) `December 2015's index` `the December indices since`
                     DIVIDED BY `December 2015's index`)

#ASSERT `the 2016 shekel supplement updated by the index` 100 100 (LIST 101, 100.5) EQUALS 101
#ASSERT `the 2016 shekel supplement updated by the index` 100 100 (LIST 99, 100.5) EQUALS 100.5

-- 10.6: not counted toward the minimum-wage top-up, an "excluded
-- supplement" for the 2015 temporary provision. 10.7: salary for every
-- purpose — the hour value, overtime and the rest of 6.2(1), severance,
-- pensions, pension and training-fund contributions and every other
-- contribution usual on the combined salary. 10.8: not in the base of any
-- supplement existing on the eve of the signing (future ones by their own
-- rules). 10.9: the Government states that, by §8 of the State Service
-- (Pensions) Law, it is in the determining salary.
DECLARE `what a 2016 framework supplement might count for` IS ONE OF
    `the 2016 framework's minimum-wage top-up`
    `the 2016 framework's hour value and overtime`
    `the 2016 framework's severance pay`
    `the 2016 framework's pensions and pension contributions`
    `the 2016 framework's training fund and other contributions`
    `the base of a supplement existing on 18.4.2016`
    `the 2016 framework's determining salary`

@ref akn:art_10__para_10-6 akn:art_10__para_10-7 akn:art_10__para_10-8 akn:art_10__para_10-9
GIVEN p IS A `what a 2016 framework supplement might count for`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2016 shekel supplement counts for` p IF
        NOT p EQUALS `the 2016 framework's minimum-wage top-up`
    AND NOT p EQUALS `the base of a supplement existing on 18.4.2016`

-- 10.10: 11.3 (salary data) reaches too the data each employer holds that
-- bears on the sum, if the Histadrut asks by 30.4.2016.
@ref akn:art_10__para_10-10
`the last day to ask for the 2016 shekel supplement's data` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 30 4 2016

-- 10.11: a mistake found in the sum (too high or too low) is corrected in
-- the salary paid after it is known, back to the day the sum fell due.
@ref akn:art_10__para_10-11
`correcting the 2016 shekel sum` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `correct a mistake in the 2016 shekel supplement in the next salary`

-- 10.12: disputes over the sum go to the follow-up committee alone.
@ref akn:art_10__para_10-12
`a dispute over the 2016 shekel sum goes only to the follow-up committee` MEANS TRUE

-- 10.13: paid from the salary for July 2016, at the latest from August's,
-- with July's differences (convention dates.salary-month).
@ref akn:art_10__para_10-13
`paying the 2016 shekel supplement` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the 2016 shekel supplement from the July 2016 salary`
    LEST  (PARTY `the employer`
           MUST  `pay the July 2016 differences with the August 2016 salary`)

§§ `11 משא ומתן נוסף ודירוגים ייחודיים`

-- akn:art_11 The heading of §11.

-- 11.1: the cost of 5.1.2–5.1.5, less §9's cost, is allocated by the
-- default of §§12–15, or by another division a collective agreement
-- between the parties sets, provided it narrows the gaps within the group
-- as a whole and has the wages commissioner's express written approval in
-- advance. 11.4: absent such an agreement the default governs, it takes
-- nothing from industrial peace (§25), and no dispute is declared and no
-- organisational measure taken for want of an approved agreement.
@ref akn:art_11__para_11-1 akn:art_11__para_11-4
GIVEN `an agreement allocates it` IS A BOOLEAN, `it narrows the group's gaps` IS A BOOLEAN, `approved in advance in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a 2016 step is allocated by agreement, not by default` `an agreement allocates it` `it narrows the group's gaps` `approved in advance in writing` IF
    `an agreement allocates it` AND `it narrows the group's gaps` AND `approved in advance in writing`

`no dispute for want of an approved 2016 allocation` MEANS
    PARTY `the New General Histadrut`
    SHANT `declare a dispute or take measures for want of an approved allocation`

-- 11.2: soon after the signing the employers negotiate, with each union,
-- a collective agreement for each calculation group it represents, to
-- carry out §§5–8 — save 5.1.1's cost (paid by §10) and §9's; ¶2: for an
-- employer under §29 of the Budget Foundations Law, subject to it.
@ref akn:art_11__para_11-2 akn:art_11__para_11-2/p2
`negotiating the allocation of the 2016 frame` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `negotiate an agreement allocating the 2016 cost frame`

`the parts of the 2016 frame left to negotiation` MEANS LIST "5.1.2", "5.1.3", "5.1.4", "5.1.5"

-- 11.3: each employer gives the Histadrut the salary data it holds that
-- bear on the negotiation and that it asks for, by law (the Privacy
-- Protection Law among them; no identifying details); ¶2: as the employer
-- holds it, unprocessed; ¶3: a request that needs processing the employer
-- finds reasonable it examines favourably, tells the Histadrut the
-- estimated cost, and produces the data if the Histadrut agrees to bear
-- it; otherwise the request goes no further.
@ref akn:art_11__para_11-3 akn:art_11__para_11-3/p2 akn:art_11__para_11-3/p3
`transferring the salary data under the 2016 framework` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `transfer the salary data the Histadrut asks for under the 2016 framework`

GIVEN `the processing is reasonable to the employer` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Histadrut bears the cost` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `processed data is produced under the 2016 framework` `the processing is reasonable to the employer` `the Histadrut bears the cost` IF
    `the processing is reasonable to the employer` AND `the Histadrut bears the cost`

-- 11.5: the special scales of the State's service (the border crossings,
-- the judges' typists, Yahalom, the land authority): further to 7.2(ג), the
-- whole cost is divided among them by annex ד'; no 2016 percentage
-- supplement is paid them and 11.1, 11.2 and §§12–15 do not reach them;
-- the typists, Yahalom and the land authority have the 2016 shekel
-- supplement as the annex sets it, and in the border crossings' updated
-- basic table the whole frame is allocated. ¶3: unless the parties agree
-- otherwise.
@ref akn:art_11__para_11-5 akn:art_11__para_11-5/p2 akn:art_11__para_11-5/p3
GIVEN scale IS A STRING, `the parties agreed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the defaults of §§12–15 reach the scale` scale `the parties agreed otherwise` IF
    `the parties agreed otherwise` OR NOT elem scale `the special scales of the State's service`

§§ `12–15 ברירות המחדל להקצאת העלות`

-- akn:art_12 The heading of §12.
-- akn:art_13 The heading of §13.
-- akn:art_14 The heading of §14.
-- akn:art_15 The heading of §15.

-- §12 ¶1: where by 31.12.2016 no agreement under 11.1 allocates 5.1.2's
-- cost for a group, then on 1.3.2017 1.75% of §6's base is allocated to it:
-- a percentage supplement of 1.375% (12.1), and the rest to raise the 2016
-- shekel supplement (12.2); no further negotiation on that cost. §§13–15
-- the same for the later steps: by 31.10.2017, from 1.1.2018, 1.5%, the
-- percentage supplement +0.75% (to 2.125%); by 31.3.2018, from 1.6.2018,
-- 1.75%, +0.875% (to 3%); by 30.9.2018, from 1.12.2018, 1.5%, +0.75% (to
-- 3.75%) — each "in addition", with the rest of the rules unchanged.
@desc A default of §§12–15: the step it allocates, the day, the cost (D), and the percentage supplement it adds.
DECLARE `2016 framework default` HAS
    `the default's step`           IS A STRING
    `the agreement's last day`     IS A DATE
    `the default's day`            IS A DATE
    `the default's cost`           IS A NUMBER
    `the percentage it adds`       IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:art_12/p1 akn:art_13/p1 akn:art_13__para_a akn:art_13__para_a/p2 akn:art_14/p1 akn:art_14__para_a akn:art_14__para_a/p2 akn:art_15/p1 akn:art_15__para_a akn:art_15__para_a/p2
`the defaults of the 2016 framework` MEANS
    LIST `2016 framework default` "5.1.2" (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2016) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2017) (1.75%) (1.375%),
         `2016 framework default` "5.1.3" (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 10 2017) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2018) (1.5%) (0.75%),
         `2016 framework default` "5.1.4" (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 2018) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2018) (1.75%) (0.875%),
         `2016 framework default` "5.1.5" (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 9 2018) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2018) (1.5%) (0.75%)

-- Each default's cost is what its step of §5.1 adds, on the same day.
GIVEN f IS A `2016 framework default`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a 2016 default is its step` f IF
    any (GIVEN s YIELD     s's `the step's clause` EQUALS f's `the default's step`
                       AND s's `the step's day` EQUALS f's `the default's day`
                       AND `what a 2016 framework step adds` s EQUALS f's `the default's cost`)
        `the steps of the 2016 framework`

#ASSERT all `a 2016 default is its step` `the defaults of the 2016 framework`

-- 12.1(א): "תוספת אחוזית 2016", the same rate for every employee in every
-- grade; with §§13(א), 14(א) and 15(א) it is, in a group no agreement
-- reached, 1.375% from 1.3.2017, 2.125% from 1.1.2018, 3% from 1.6.2018 and
-- 3.75% from 1.12.2018 — each default by its own step, as the group's
-- agreements stand.
@ref akn:art_12__para_12-1 akn:art_12__para_12-1__subpara_a
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the steps agreed in time` IS A LIST OF STRING @desc the clauses of 5.1.2–5.1.5 an agreement allocated for the group by its last day
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2016 percentage supplement rate by default on` d `the steps agreed in time` IS
    sum (map (GIVEN f YIELD f's `the percentage it adds`)
             (filter (GIVEN f YIELD     d `is on or after` (f's `the default's day`)
                                    AND NOT elem (f's `the default's step`) `the steps agreed in time`)
                     `the defaults of the 2016 framework`))

#ASSERT `the 2016 percentage supplement rate by default on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2017) EMPTY EQUALS 1.375%
#ASSERT `the 2016 percentage supplement rate by default on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2018) EMPTY EQUALS 2.125%
#ASSERT `the 2016 percentage supplement rate by default on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2018) EMPTY EQUALS 3%
#ASSERT `the 2016 percentage supplement rate by default on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2018) EMPTY EQUALS 3.75%
#ASSERT `the 2016 percentage supplement rate by default on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 2017) EMPTY EQUALS 0

-- 12.1(ב): its base is the combined salary, seniority and every
-- cost-of-living increment paid until it is paid, and every supplement
-- (percentage and shekel) existing on 31.12.2015 and counted for the hour
-- value, save (1) those not paid monthly, weekly or daily, (2) those with
-- another updating mechanism, (3) the minimum-wage top-up, (4) the 2016
-- shekel supplement or any other paid from this agreement's cost; ¶2: 6.5
-- stands. (ג): so it is no base for the supplements of 31.12.2015 (they are
-- in its base).
@desc A pay component, as 12.1(ב) asks about it.
DECLARE `component of the 2016 percentage base` HAS
    `a base salary component`                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc the combined salary, seniority, a cost-of-living increment
    `a supplement existing on 31.12.2015`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `counted for the hour value, for 12.1`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `paid monthly, weekly or daily, for 12.1` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has another updating mechanism`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the minimum-wage top-up, for 12.1`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `paid from the 2016 framework's cost`     IS A BOOLEAN

@ref akn:art_12__para_12-1__subpara_b akn:art_12__para_12-1__subpara_b__cls_1 akn:art_12__para_12-1__subpara_b__cls_2 akn:art_12__para_12-1__subpara_b__cls_3 akn:art_12__para_12-1__subpara_b__cls_4 akn:art_12__para_12-1__subpara_b/p2 akn:art_12__para_12-1__subpara_c
GIVEN c IS A `component of the 2016 percentage base`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in the base of the 2016 percentage supplement` c IF
        NOT c's `paid from the 2016 framework's cost`
    AND NOT c's `the minimum-wage top-up, for 12.1`
    AND (   c's `a base salary component`
         OR (    c's `a supplement existing on 31.12.2015`
             AND c's `counted for the hour value, for 12.1`
             AND c's `paid monthly, weekly or daily, for 12.1`
             AND NOT c's `has another updating mechanism`))

`the framework's 2016 percentage supplement is a base for the supplements of 31.12.2015` MEANS FALSE

-- 12.1(ד): not toward the minimum-wage top-up, an excluded supplement;
-- (ה): salary for every purpose, as 10.7 says of the shekel supplement;
-- (ו): in the annual supplements and grants computed on the hour-value
-- salary or the budgetary pension's determining salary; (ז): the
-- Government's statement that it is in the determining salary.
@ref akn:art_12__para_12-1__subpara_d akn:art_12__para_12-1__subpara_e akn:art_12__para_12-1__subpara_f akn:art_12__para_12-1__subpara_g
GIVEN p IS A `what a 2016 framework supplement might count for`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the framework's 2016 percentage supplement counts for` p IF
        NOT p EQUALS `the 2016 framework's minimum-wage top-up`
    AND NOT p EQUALS `the base of a supplement existing on 18.4.2016`

`the framework's 2016 percentage supplement is in the annual supplements on the hour-value salary` MEANS TRUE

-- 12.2: the rest of the cost (C) raises the 2016 shekel supplement from
-- 1.3.2017, its rules unchanged, by the one sum that makes A + B = C — A
-- and B as in 10.2, for the rise; C = D − E: D, 1.75% of §6's base for the
-- group, without the special supplements and their effect on 6.2(1)–(2);
-- E, the cost given to 12.1's percentage supplement with its effect on
-- 6.2(1)–(2). (ג): the percentage base is smaller than §6's and leaves out
-- the minimum-wage top-up, so what the percentage does not take goes to
-- the shekel rise, and all of 5.1.2's cost is divided. §§13(ב), 14(ב) and
-- 15(ב): the same for each later step, with D at that step's cost and E
-- that step's percentage rise; and (ג) of each with its own step of 5.1.
@ref akn:art_12__para_12-2 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_a akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_b akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_b/p2 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_b/p3 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_b/p4 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_b/p5 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_b/p6 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_b/p7 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_b/p8 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_b/p9 akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_c akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_c/p2 akn:art_13__para_b akn:art_13__para_b/p2 akn:art_13__para_b/p3 akn:art_13__para_b/p4 akn:art_13__para_b/p5 akn:art_13__para_b/p6 akn:art_13__para_b/p7 akn:art_13__para_b/p8 akn:art_13__para_b/p9 akn:art_13__para_b/p10 akn:art_14__para_b akn:art_14__para_b/p2 akn:art_14__para_b/p3 akn:art_14__para_b/p4 akn:art_14__para_b/p5 akn:art_14__para_b/p6 akn:art_14__para_b/p7 akn:art_14__para_b/p8 akn:art_15__para_b akn:art_15__para_b/p2 akn:art_15__para_b/p3 akn:art_15__para_b/p4 akn:art_15__para_b/p5 akn:art_15__para_b/p6 akn:art_15__para_b/p7 akn:art_15__para_b/p8 akn:art_15__para_b/p9 akn:art_15__para_b/p10
GIVEN f IS A `2016 framework default`
      `the group's base without the special supplements and their effect` IS A NUMBER
      E IS A NUMBER @desc the cost of the default's percentage rise, with its effect on 6.2(1)–(2)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `C of a 2016 default's shekel rise` f `the group's base without the special supplements and their effect` E IS
    `not below zero` ((f's `the default's cost`) TIMES `the group's base without the special supplements and their effect` MINUS E)

GIVEN f IS A `2016 framework default`
      base IS A NUMBER
      E IS A NUMBER
      `the group's full-position months in 2015` IS A NUMBER
      `the growth of 6.2(1)–(2) per shekel` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a 2016 default's shekel rise` f base E `the group's full-position months in 2015` `the growth of 6.2(1)–(2) per shekel` IS
    `the shekel sum that makes A + B = C` (`C of a 2016 default's shekel rise` f base E) `the group's full-position months in 2015` `the growth of 6.2(1)–(2) per shekel`

-- The whole of a step's cost is divided: E plus what the shekel rise
-- costs is D.
`the first default of 2016` MEANS
    `2016 framework default` "5.1.2" (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2016) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2017) (1.75%) (1.375%)

`an example default's shekel rise` MEANS
    `a 2016 default's shekel rise` `the first default of 2016` 12000000 150000 1500 100

`what the example default divides` MEANS
    `an example default's shekel rise` TIMES (1500 PLUS 100) PLUS 150000

#ASSERT `what the example default divides` EQUALS 1.75% TIMES 12000000

-- 12.1(ח), 12.2(ד), 13(ג), 14(ג), 15(ג): each default is paid from the
-- salary of its month, at the latest with the next month's, the first
-- month's differences with it (convention dates.salary-month).
@ref akn:art_12__para_12-1__subpara_h akn:art_12__para_12-2__subpara_d akn:art_13__para_c akn:art_14__para_c akn:art_15__para_c
GIVEN f IS A `2016 framework default`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `the salary months a 2016 default is paid with` f IS
    LIST (DATE_YEAR (f's `the default's day`) TIMES 12 PLUS DATE_MONTH (f's `the default's day`)),
         (DATE_YEAR (f's `the default's day`) TIMES 12 PLUS DATE_MONTH (f's `the default's day`) PLUS 1)

`paying a 2016 default` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay a default allocation of the 2016 framework from its salary month`

§§ `16 הקדמת הגדלת תוספות צמודות מדד`

-- akn:art_16 The heading of §16.

-- 16.1: as no new cost-of-living increments were agreed for over a decade,
-- the supplements set to be updated by the index on the days a
-- cost-of-living increment is paid are raised on the frame's days and to
-- its figures — 1%, to 2.75%, to 4.25%, to 6%, to 7.5% — of "the base of
-- the supplement", its sum on the eve of the signing. 16.2: that is an
-- advance of the update their own agreement requires, counted on its next
-- days, so there is no double update.
@ref akn:art_16__para_16-1 akn:art_16__para_16-1/p2 akn:art_16__para_16-1/p3 akn:art_16__para_16-1/p4 akn:art_16__para_16-1/p5 akn:art_16__para_16-1/p6 akn:art_16__para_16-1/p7
GIVEN d IS A DATE, `the base of the supplement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `an index-linked supplement brought forward on` d `the base of the supplement` IS
    `the base of the supplement` `increased by` (`the 2016 framework allocation on` d)

@ref akn:art_16__para_16-2
GIVEN `the index update its agreement requires` IS A NUMBER, `the advance under §16` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `what an index update adds after §16's advance` `the index update its agreement requires` `the advance under §16` IS
    `not below zero` (`the index update its agreement requires` MINUS `the advance under §16`)

#ASSERT `an index-linked supplement brought forward on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2017) 200 EQUALS `a special supplement of 2016 on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2017) 200

§§ `17–18 טכנולוגיות חדשות וחופשת הורים בסוף אוגוסט`

-- akn:art_17 The heading of §17.
-- akn:art_18 The heading of §18.

-- §17: the Histadrut declares for new technologies and will cooperate in
-- bringing them in; that takes nothing from its and the employees' rights
-- where they bear on the employees (each side keeping its means); a
-- dispute on the matter needs the approval of the Histadrut's coordination
-- and execution committee, and the chair of the trade union division
-- accompanies its resolution as needed.
@ref akn:art_17/p1
`the Histadrut cooperates in new technologies` MEANS TRUE

GIVEN `the coordination and execution committee approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a dispute over new technologies may be declared` `the coordination and execution committee approved` IF
    `the coordination and execution committee approved`

-- 18.1: "a working parent" meets all of: (18.1.1) entitled to a shorter
-- day under Takshir 31.152 or 31.153 and working it; (18.1.2) his yearly
-- leave from his employer is no more than 22 days in a five-day office or
-- 26 in a six-day one — every kind of annual leave counted (special,
-- casual and the like), not days of choice; sick leave, training days and
-- personal-event days (mourning) are not leave for this; (18.1.3) no other
-- benefit from his employer on leave in 1 July–31 August (a concentrated
-- leave charging fewer days than he is away, for example); (18.1.4) one of:
-- (1) the spouse works, employed or self-employed, and has not used a like
-- benefit at work (the employee declares it, a condition of the right),
-- (2) the child is in his sole custody, (3) the child is in his sole care
-- for the spouse's disability or illness, a doctor confirming in writing
-- that the spouse cannot care for the child.
@desc A worker, as §18 of the 2016 framework asks about him.
DECLARE `2016 framework parent` HAS
    `entitled to a shorter day under Takshir 31.152 or 31.153 and working it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `entitled to the shorter day under Takshir 31.152` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a parent under Takshir 31.153(א)(1)–(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `yearly leave days` IS A NUMBER @desc every kind of annual leave, not days of choice, sick leave, training or personal-event days
    `in a six-day office` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has another leave benefit in July and August` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the spouse works and has not used a like benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `declared the spouse's work` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the child is in his sole custody` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the child is in his sole care, a doctor confirming the spouse cannot care` IS A BOOLEAN
    `works in shifts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `his position` IS A NUMBER
    `his working day in hours` IS A NUMBER
    `his working days a week by his position` IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:art_18__para_18-1 akn:art_18__para_18-1__subpara_18-1-2 akn:art_18__para_18-1__subpara_18-1-2__cls_a akn:art_18__para_18-1__subpara_18-1-2__cls_b akn:art_18__para_18-1__subpara_18-1-2/p2 akn:art_18__para_18-1__subpara_18-1-3 akn:art_18__para_18-1__subpara_18-1-4 akn:art_18__para_18-1__subpara_18-1-4__cls_1 akn:art_18__para_18-1__subpara_18-1-4__cls_1/p2 akn:art_18__para_18-1__subpara_18-1-4__cls_2 akn:art_18__para_18-1__subpara_18-1-4__cls_3
GIVEN w IS A `2016 framework parent`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets 18.1.2–18.1.4 of the 2016 framework` w IF
        w's `yearly leave days` AT MOST (IF w's `in a six-day office` THEN 26 ELSE 22)
    AND NOT w's `has another leave benefit in July and August`
    AND (   (w's `the spouse works and has not used a like benefit` AND w's `declared the spouse's work`)
         OR w's `the child is in his sole custody`
         OR w's `the child is in his sole care, a doctor confirming the spouse cannot care`)

@ref akn:art_18__para_18-1__subpara_18-1-1
GIVEN w IS A `2016 framework parent`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a working parent under the 2016 framework` w IF
        w's `entitled to a shorter day under Takshir 31.152 or 31.153 and working it`
    AND `meets 18.1.2–18.1.4 of the 2016 framework` w

-- 18.2: a working parent has his day shortened by an hour on each of the
-- last ten working days of August that fall on Sunday to Thursday, ten
-- hours in all ("the parents' special leave hours"). 18.3: with the
-- employer's consent and coordinated in advance he may take them otherwise,
-- in one day or several, from 1 August to 30 September of that year ("the
-- period of use"); ¶2: so too where the work did not let him take them as
-- 18.2 says.
@ref akn:art_18__para_18-2 akn:art_18__para_18-2/p1 akn:art_18__para_18-3 akn:art_18__para_18-3/p2
`the parents' special leave hours` MEANS 10
`the days the parents' hour is taken on` MEANS 10

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
DECIDE `the period of use in` y IS
    LIST DATE_FROM_DMY 1 8 y, DATE_FROM_DMY 30 9 y

-- 18.3 ¶3 (the heading of 18.4) and 18.4: one who is (18.4.1) a parent in
-- a case of Takshir 31.153(א)(1)–(3) and (18.4.2) meets 18.1 save 18.1.1
-- (not entitled to the shorter day, or not working it) has, in place of
-- the hours, one day's leave at the employer's cost ("a parents' day");
-- ¶2: in shifts or part-time, as 18.5 or 18.6 adjust it.
@ref akn:art_18__para_18-3/p3 akn:art_18__para_18-4 akn:art_18__para_18-4__subpara_18-4-1 akn:art_18__para_18-4__subpara_18-4-2 akn:art_18__para_18-4/p2
GIVEN w IS A `2016 framework parent`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has a parents' day under the 2016 framework` w IF
        w's `a parent under Takshir 31.153(א)(1)–(3)`
    AND NOT w's `entitled to a shorter day under Takshir 31.152 or 31.153 and working it`
    AND `meets 18.1.2–18.1.4 of the 2016 framework` w

-- 18.5: one of 18.4 in shifts at a full position has a parents' day as
-- long as his usual working day, at most 8 hours; ¶3: one whose day is
-- longer adds hours from his accrued annual leave to make up a day. 18.6:
-- one of 18.4 in shifts at part time, and one of 18.2 at part time (save
-- one entitled under 31.152), has in place of the hours: (א) working five
-- days in a five-day office or six in a six-day one, one day's leave; (ב)
-- working fewer, part of a day: (1) his days a week over 5, (2) over 6.
@ref akn:art_18__para_18-5 akn:art_18__para_18-5/p2 akn:art_18__para_18-5/p3
GIVEN w IS A `2016 framework parent`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the hours of a full-time shift worker's parents' day` w IS
    IF w's `his working day in hours` GREATER THAN 8 THEN 8 ELSE w's `his working day in hours`

GIVEN w IS A `2016 framework parent`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the leave hours a shift worker adds to his parents' day` w IS
    `not below zero` (w's `his working day in hours` MINUS 8)

@ref akn:art_18__para_18-6 akn:art_18__para_18-6/p2 akn:art_18__para_18-6__subpara_a akn:art_18__para_18-6__subpara_b akn:art_18__para_18-6__subpara_b__cls_1 akn:art_18__para_18-6__subpara_b__cls_2
GIVEN w IS A `2016 framework parent`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the part-time parents' leave in days` w IS
    IF w's `in a six-day office`
    THEN (IF w's `his working days a week by his position` AT LEAST 6 THEN 1 ELSE w's `his working days a week by his position` DIVIDED BY 6)
    ELSE (IF w's `his working days a week by his position` AT LEAST 5 THEN 1 ELSE w's `his working days a week by his position` DIVIDED BY 5)

#ASSERT `the part-time parents' leave in days` (`2016 framework parent` FALSE FALSE TRUE 20 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0.6 5 3) EQUALS 0.6

-- 18.7 (its heading, and ¶1): leave under §18 is taken in the period of
-- use only, as the employee chooses, coordinated in advance; it cannot be
-- accrued or redeemed, even unused for any reason. ¶2: the need to
-- coordinate and the employer's consent take nothing from the employer's
-- duty to let an entitled employee who wants it use it in that period.
@ref akn:art_18__para_18-7 akn:art_18__para_18-7/p1 akn:art_18__para_18-7/p2
`parents' leave can be accrued or redeemed` MEANS FALSE

`letting a parent use the leave` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `let a parent use the parents' leave in the period of use`

-- 18.8: the shortened day under §18 is no shortening that takes away the
-- shorter day of Takshir 31.153.
@ref akn:art_18__para_18-8
`§18's shorter day takes away Takshir 31.153's` MEANS FALSE

§§ `19 גמלאים בפנסיה תקציבית`

-- akn:art_19 The heading of §19.

-- 19.1: the Treasury will circulate a bill amending the State Service
-- (Pensions) Law (the Pensions Law) on these principles. 19.1.1: it reaches
-- one who retired under it from 1 January 2013 to 30 November 2018 and was
-- graded, on the eve, in a scale of annex ה' ("an eligible retiree").
@ref akn:art_19__para_19-1
`circulating the 2016 pensions bill` MEANS
    PARTY `the Treasury`
    MUST  `circulate the bill amending the Pensions Law under the 2016 framework`

@ref akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_19-1-1
GIVEN `retired on` IS A DATE, `in an annex ה' scale on the eve` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an eligible retiree under the 2016 framework` `retired on` `in an annex ה' scale on the eve` IF
        `retired on` `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2013)
    AND `retired on` `is on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 11 2018)
    AND `in an annex ה' scale on the eve`

-- 19.1.2: by the amendment the determining salary (for the pension) of an
-- eligible retiree or his survivors grows by Y = X·A + X·B·C: X, the
-- retiree's coefficient for his month of retirement in annex ו'; A, the
-- full shekel supplement paid under this agreement or one of §11 to an
-- employee of the retiree's grade on the eve (§8 of the Pensions Law); for
-- a border-crossings retiree, the whole shekel sum by which this agreement
-- raised the basic salary of his grade (the whole frame being in it); B,
-- the full percentage supplement so paid; C, his determining salary under
-- the Pensions Law save (א) havraa and clothing pay, (ב) supplements with
-- another mechanism than the cost-of-living agreements, (ג) the minimum-wage
-- top-up, (ד) supplements first paid after 31.12.2015, this agreement's
-- among them.
@ref akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_19-1-2 akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_19-1-2/p2 akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_19-1-2/p3 akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_19-1-2/p4 akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_19-1-2/p5 akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_19-1-2/p6 akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_19-1-2/p7 akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_19-1-2__cls_a akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_19-1-2__cls_b akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_19-1-2__cls_c akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_19-1-2__cls_d
GIVEN X IS A NUMBER, `A of 19.1.2` IS A NUMBER, `B of 19.1.2` IS A NUMBER, `C of 19.1.2` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Y under 19.1.2 of the 2016 framework` X `A of 19.1.2` `B of 19.1.2` `C of 19.1.2` IS
    X TIMES `A of 19.1.2` PLUS X TIMES `B of 19.1.2` TIMES `C of 19.1.2`

#ASSERT `Y under 19.1.2 of the 2016 framework` (70%) 264.53 (3.75%) 10000 EQUALS 70% TIMES 264.53 PLUS 70% TIMES 375

-- 19.1.3: where several shekel (A) or percentage (B) supplements of this
-- agreement, or of it and another, are relevant, the formula runs on each
-- apart and Y is the sum. 19.1.4: where an existing shekel supplement of
-- active employees is raised under this agreement or one of §11, A is the
-- whole rise; so B for a percentage supplement raised.
@ref akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_19-1-3 akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_19-1-3/p2 akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_19-1-4
GIVEN X IS A NUMBER
      `the shekel sums or rises` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the percentage rates or rises` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `C of 19.1.2` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Y summed under 19.1.3 of the 2016 framework` X `the shekel sums or rises` `the percentage rates or rises` `C of 19.1.2` IS
    sum (map (GIVEN sh YIELD X TIMES sh) `the shekel sums or rises`)
    PLUS sum (map (GIVEN pc YIELD X TIMES pc TIMES `C of 19.1.2`) `the percentage rates or rises`)

-- 19.1.5: the rise is made gradually, on the dates of annex ו'.
@ref akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_19-1-5
`the 2016 pensioners' rise is gradual by annex ו'` MEANS TRUE

-- 19.1.6: and to one who retired from 1 March 2013 to 30 November 2018
-- graded on the eve in the land authority's scale — in place of 19.1.2–
-- 19.1.5: where, but for chapter ג'2 of the Pensions Law, his salary on the
-- eve of retirement would pass the salary ceiling (§§63יד, 63יג), the
-- pension is recomputed from annex ו''s dates as if the ceiling were
-- higher by Y = X·3.75·A + X·B: X as above; A, his basic salary for the
-- month of his retirement or June 2016, the earlier, with study pay א' or
-- ב' or management pay he had in it; B, the full 2016 shekel supplement
-- for his grade. ¶7: Y grows in steps with X, on annex ו''s dates.
@ref akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_19-1-6 akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_19-1-6/p2 akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_19-1-6/p3 akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_19-1-6/p4 akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_19-1-6/p5 akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_19-1-6/p6 akn:art_19__para_19-1__subpara_19-1-6/p7
GIVEN `retired on` IS A DATE, `in the land authority's scale on the eve` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an eligible land-authority retiree under the 2016 framework` `retired on` `in the land authority's scale on the eve` IF
        `retired on` `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2013)
    AND `retired on` `is on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 11 2018)
    AND `in the land authority's scale on the eve`

GIVEN X IS A NUMBER, `A of 19.1.6` IS A NUMBER, `B of 19.1.6` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Y under 19.1.6 of the 2016 framework` X `A of 19.1.6` `B of 19.1.6` IS
    X TIMES 3.75 TIMES `A of 19.1.6` PLUS X TIMES `B of 19.1.6`

-- 19.2: the Histadrut declares that (19.2.1) the bill's principles are
-- acceptable and it will support the legislation as needed, and (19.2.2)
-- once the Knesset passes it, it has no demand to raise the determining
-- salary, or for a further supplement or benefit, for the rises of this
-- agreement, of one of §11, or of the agreements signed beside it, or for
-- the time to 31.12.2017.
@ref akn:art_19__para_19-2 akn:art_19__para_19-2__subpara_19-2-1 akn:art_19__para_19-2__subpara_19-2-2 akn:art_19__para_19-2__subpara_19-2-2/p2
GIVEN `the Knesset passed the amendment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `2016 framework action`
DECIDE `the Histadrut's 2016 pension undertakings` `the Knesset passed the amendment` IS
    IF `the Knesset passed the amendment`
    THEN PARTY `the New General Histadrut`
         SHANT `demand a further rise of the determining salary for the 2016 frame`
    ELSE PARTY `the New General Histadrut`
         MAY   `support the bill amending the Pensions Law under the 2016 framework`

-- 19.3: between the Histadrut and each employer among whom the Pensions
-- Law applies by law, agreement or arrangement (of the signatories: the
-- Centre of Local Government, the three cities, the regional councils, the
-- religious councils, the NII, the Employment Service and Israel Post), the
-- amendment applies to them on the same rules and dates, to their scales of
-- annex ה', and — with the wages commissioner's approval — to the
-- neighbourhood and settlement rabbis, the local authorities' youth
-- education scale and their other scales the State has not.
@ref akn:art_19__para_19-3
`the signatories §19.3 of 2016 reaches` MEANS
    LIST "מרכז השלטון המקומי", "שלוש הערים הגדולות", "מרכז המועצות האזוריות", "חבר המועצות הדתיות", "המוסד לביטוח לאומי", "שירות התעסוקה", "חברת דואר ישראל בע\"מ"

GIVEN scale IS A STRING, `in annex ה'` IS A BOOLEAN, `a scale the State has` IS A BOOLEAN, `the wages commissioner approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2016 pensions amendment reaches a scale of a §19.3 employer` scale `in annex ה'` `a scale the State has` `the wages commissioner approved` IF
        `in annex ה'`
    OR ((NOT `a scale the State has`) AND `the wages commissioner approved`)

-- 19.4: an employer §19.3 does not reach but with a budgetary pension by
-- agreement or arrangement (of the signatories: the Hebrew University and
-- the Technion) applies the amendment to a retiree of 19.1.1's terms, with
-- the adjustments needed and the wages commissioner's approval.
@ref akn:art_19__para_19-4
`the signatories §19.4 of 2016 reaches` MEANS LIST "האוניברסיטה העברית", "הטכניון"

-- 19.5: an eligible retiree entitled to a jubilee grant (Takshir 25.5 and
-- its parallels; ¶3), or his survivors, has the salary its component is
-- computed on raised by Y, gradually as 19.1.5 says, if Y's supplements
-- count for the hour value; ¶2: a land-authority retiree recomputed under
-- 19.1.6 has his jubilee grant recomputed so too. ¶4: the day the jubilee
-- component is paid does not change.
@ref akn:art_19__para_19-5 akn:art_19__para_19-5/p2 akn:art_19__para_19-5/p3 akn:art_19__para_19-5/p4
GIVEN Y IS A NUMBER, `Y's supplements count for the hour value` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the jubilee grant base's rise under the 2016 framework` Y `Y's supplements count for the hour value` IS
    IF `Y's supplements count for the hour value` THEN Y ELSE 0

`§19.5 changes when the jubilee component is paid` MEANS FALSE

-- 19.6: §19 is not relevant to employers without a budgetary pension; no
-- other benefit is given them or their employees for it, nor claimed.
@ref akn:art_19__para_19-6
GIVEN `the employer has a budgetary pension` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `2016 framework action`
DECIDE `a benefit for §19's cost of 2016` `the employer has a budgetary pension` IS
    IF `the employer has a budgetary pension`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the employer`
         SHANT `give another benefit for the 2016 pensioners' rise`

-- 19.7: §19 is no approval under §29 of the Budget Foundations Law of a
-- benefit against it, the computation of the determining salary, the
-- pension or a jubilee grant among them.
@ref akn:art_19__para_19-7
`§19 of the 2016 framework is an approval under §29` MEANS FALSE

`why the Pensions Law is not in the 2016 framework` MEANS
    `outside the corpus` "חוק שירות המדינה (גמלאות) [נוסח משולב], התש\"ל-1970, ותקנון שירות המדינה"

§§ `20–22 הרשויות המקומיות, הסכם גמול מומחיות ומבנה העסקה`

-- akn:art_20 The heading of §20.
-- akn:art_21 The heading of §21.
-- akn:art_22 The heading of §22.

-- 20.1: the Centre of Local Government, the three cities and the regional
-- councils agree with the Histadrut that 5.1.1's and 5.1.2's cost for the
-- uniform scale and the academics (psychologists out, and those of both
-- scales in the cities' hospitals: "the uniform and academic employees")
-- is allocated as a collective agreement signed by 30.6.16 sets, narrowing
-- the group's gaps as a whole, with the wages commissioner's express
-- written approval in advance.
@ref akn:art_20__para_20-1 akn:art_20__para_20-1/p2
`the last day for the local authorities' allocation agreement` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2016

-- 20.2: by §ט.9 of the agreement of 17.5.2012 on the frame of 2009–2012
-- in those authorities ("the Ma'of agreement"), the frame of the uniform
-- and academic employees is cut by 0.075% to 7.425%, from 5.1.1's
-- allocation, so that it is 0.925% in place of 1%.
@ref akn:art_20__para_20-2
`the Ma'of cut of the 2016 frame` MEANS 0.075%

`the local authorities' uniform and academic frame` MEANS
    `the 2016 framework cost frame in all` MINUS `the Ma'of cut of the 2016 frame`

`the local authorities' 5.1.1 allocation` MEANS 1% MINUS `the Ma'of cut of the 2016 frame`

#ASSERT `the local authorities' uniform and academic frame` EQUALS 7.425%
#ASSERT `the local authorities' 5.1.1 allocation` EQUALS 0.925%

-- 20.3: so for the uniform and academic employees: (א) for 5.1.1's cost
-- §7's computation is joint, for the rest as §7 says; (ב) "on 1.7.2017"
-- §10 (the 2016 shekel supplement) does not apply — F-framework-2016-b:
-- the shekel supplement starts on 1.7.2016, and (ד) brings it back to them
-- from 1.7.2016; read 1.7.2016 (convention dates.misprinted-year, a pick
-- put to the lawyer in MMS-486); (ג) the
-- negotiation of §11 is on the whole frame less §9's cost, not 5.1.2–5.1.5
-- alone; (ד) if by 31.12.2016 no approved agreement is reached, from
-- 1.3.2017 5.1.1's cut cost is allocated by §10 back to 1.7.2016, and
-- 5.1.2's by §12; ¶2: the defaults of §§13–15 stay the defaults unless
-- agreed by their days.
@ref akn:art_20__para_20-3 akn:art_20__para_20-3__subpara_a akn:art_20__para_20-3__subpara_b akn:art_20__para_20-3__subpara_c akn:art_20__para_20-3__subpara_d akn:art_20__para_20-3__subpara_d/p2
`the day §20.3(ב) prints` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2017
`the day §20.3(ב) is read as` MEANS `the 2016 shekel supplement starts on`

`§20.3(ב) prints a day a year after the shekel supplement starts` MEANS
        DATE_SERIAL `the day §20.3(ב) prints` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the day §20.3(ב) is read as` EQUALS 365
    AND `the day §20.3(ב) is read as` EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2016

#ASSERT `§20.3(ב) prints a day a year after the shekel supplement starts`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the local authorities agreed by 31.12.2016` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `§10 reaches the uniform and academic employees on` d `the local authorities agreed by 31.12.2016` IF
        NOT `the local authorities agreed by 31.12.2016`
    AND d `is on or after` `the day §20.3(ב) is read as`

`the day §20.3(ד)'s default is paid from` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2017

-- 20.4: the youth, society and community education scale. 20.4.1: those of
-- it paid by the teaching employees' salary under the agreement of
-- 14.9.1987 have no double cost for one period — from this agreement or
-- one beside it, and from the link to the teachers' salary; where they
-- are raised for a rise of the teachers' salary in this agreement's period
-- or part of it, the cost of that rise is taken off the supplements this
-- agreement gives them, as the parties agree. 20.4.2: 20.1 reaches the
-- scale. 20.4.3: it is a calculation group of its own (§7). 20.4.4:
-- "20.3(ב) to (ה)" reach it — F-framework-2016-c: 20.3 has (א)–(ד), no
-- (ה); read (ב) to (ד) (convention reading.misprint).
@ref akn:art_20__para_20-4 akn:art_20__para_20-4__subpara_20-4-1
GIVEN `the rise under this agreement` IS A NUMBER, `the rise from the teachers' salary in the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `what a youth-education employee has from the 2016 framework` `the rise under this agreement` `the rise from the teachers' salary in the period` IS
    `not below zero` (`the rise under this agreement` MINUS `the rise from the teachers' salary in the period`)

`the agreement youth education is linked to the teachers' salary by` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 14 9 1987

@ref akn:art_20__para_20-4__subpara_20-4-2 akn:art_20__para_20-4__subpara_20-4-3 akn:art_20__para_20-4__subpara_20-4-4
`youth education is a calculation group of its own` MEANS TRUE

`the clauses of 20.3 §20.4.4 names` MEANS LIST "ב", "ג", "ד", "ה"
`the clauses 20.3 has` MEANS LIST "א", "ב", "ג", "ד"

`§20.4.4 names a clause 20.3 does not have` MEANS
    any (GIVEN c YIELD NOT elem c `the clauses 20.3 has`) `the clauses of 20.3 §20.4.4 names`

#ASSERT `§20.4.4 names a clause 20.3 does not have`

`the clauses of 20.3 that reach youth education` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN c YIELD elem c `the clauses 20.3 has`) `the clauses of 20.3 §20.4.4 names`

#ASSERT `the clauses of 20.3 that reach youth education` EQUALS LIST "ב", "ג", "ד"

-- §21: by §13 of the special agreement of 9.2.2015 on the social workers'
-- expertise pay, the social workers' frame is cut by 0.21% to 7.29%, from
-- 5.1.1's allocation — 0.79% in place of 1%, and so in C of §10.
@ref akn:art_21/p1
`the expertise-pay cut of the 2016 frame` MEANS 0.21%

`the social workers' 2016 frame` MEANS
    `the 2016 framework cost frame in all` MINUS `the expertise-pay cut of the 2016 frame`

#ASSERT `the social workers' 2016 frame` EQUALS 7.29%
#ASSERT 1% MINUS `the expertise-pay cut of the 2016 frame` EQUALS 0.79%

-- §22: 22.1 the talks on the structure of employment go on; 22.2 the
-- parties will cooperate to improve the service; 22.3 these matters are
-- not settled by this agreement, each side keeping its claims and means.
@ref akn:art_22__para_22-1 akn:art_22__para_22-2 akn:art_22__para_22-3
`going on with the structure-of-employment talks of 2016` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `go on discussing the structure of employment under the 2016 framework`

`the 2016 framework settles the structure of employment` MEANS FALSE

§§ `23–28 סכסוכים, מיצוי, שקט, הסכמים קודמים, ועדת מעקב ובוררות`

-- akn:art_23 The heading of §23.
-- akn:art_24 The heading of §24.
-- akn:art_25 The heading of §25.
-- akn:art_26 The heading of §26.
-- akn:art_27 The heading of §27.
-- akn:art_28 The heading of §28.

-- 23.1: in the State's service, the NII and the Employment Service, the
-- disputes left pending are annex ז''s, the parties' claims on them kept;
-- a claim that one was left out goes to the follow-up committee "under
-- §27 above". 23.2: at the other employers, every collective dispute,
-- national or local, on the matters it settles is void on signing. 23.3:
-- among them, void too, the dispute of 25.11.2015 on the update of
-- public-sector pay and the deadlock in the wage talks.
@ref akn:art_23__para_23-1 akn:art_23__para_23-1/p2 akn:art_23__para_23-2 akn:art_23__para_23-2/p2 akn:art_23__para_23-3
GIVEN `at the State, the NII or the Employment Service` IS A BOOLEAN, `in annex ז'` IS A BOOLEAN, `on a matter the agreement settles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a dispute stands after the 2016 framework` `at the State, the NII or the Employment Service` `in annex ז'` `on a matter the agreement settles` IF
    IF `at the State, the NII or the Employment Service`
    THEN `in annex ז'`
    ELSE NOT `on a matter the agreement settles`

`the dispute the 2016 framework names void` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 25 11 2015

-- 24.1: with the agreements signed beside it, it exhausts all the parties'
-- claims, national and local, on enlarging the frame or any further
-- benefit, for the time to 31.12.2017; 24.2: not claims pending before the
-- agreed arbitration institution or in the courts. 24.3: subject to that
-- and §11, no further negotiation on wages or benefits, at any level, for
-- that time, for the employees it covers.
@ref akn:art_24__para_24-1 akn:art_24__para_24-2 akn:art_24__para_24-3
GIVEN `pending in arbitration or a court` IS A BOOLEAN, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2016 framework exhausts the claim` `pending in arbitration or a court` d IF
        d `is on or before` `the 2016 framework agreement's period ends on`
    AND NOT `pending in arbitration or a court`

`no further wage negotiation for the time to 31.12.2017` MEANS
    PARTY `the New General Histadrut`
    SHANT `negotiate further on pay for the period to 31.12.2017`

-- §25: in the agreement's period the Histadrut does not strike against an
-- employer or a unit, in full or in part, nor harm the work in an
-- organised way, over what it settles, nationally or locally.
@ref akn:art_25/p1
`industrial peace under the 2016 framework` MEANS
    PARTY `the New General Histadrut`
    SHANT `strike or harm the work over a matter the 2016 framework settled`

-- §26: earlier terms stand for its period unless it amends or cancels
-- them, expressly or by implication.
@ref akn:art_26/p1
`earlier terms stand unless the 2016 framework changes them` MEANS TRUE

-- §27: a follow-up committee of the wages commissioner and the chair of
-- the Histadrut's trade union division goes on following and helping to
-- carry out the agreement, and decides the disagreements on it; its
-- decisions are final and bind the parties.
@ref akn:art_27/p1 akn:art_27/p2
`deciding disputes over the 2016 framework` MEANS
    PARTY `the follow-up committee`
    MUST  `decide disputes over the 2016 framework agreement`

`the 2016 follow-up committee's decisions are final` MEANS TRUE

-- §28: the agreement on the agreed arbitration institution in the public
-- services is extended until the next national wage agreement; ¶2: it
-- reaches the employers that are its parties or joined it.
@ref akn:art_28/p1 akn:art_28/p2
GIVEN d IS A DATE, `the next national wage agreement was signed on` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the arbitration institution agreement stands under the 2016 framework on` d `the next national wage agreement was signed on` IS
    CONSIDER `the next national wage agreement was signed on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST s THEN NOT d `is on or after` s

