-- Circular 2016-1-3, §1: with the January 2016 salary (paid in February),
-- at the latest February's, a one-time grant is paid. 1.א: an employee of
-- the State on the agreements of a Histadrut scale its annex א' lists,
-- employed on 1.8.2015 and continuously to 1.12.2015 ("the determining
-- period"), has 1,000; ¶2: not one in a scale of its annex ב'. 1.ב: that is
-- for a full position; a part-time employee's is in proportion to his
-- average position over 1.12.2014–30.11.2015, and (¶2) one employed in part
-- of that time, but continuously in the determining period, by the time he
-- was employed in it.
@desc An employee, as the grant circulars of 2016 ask about him.
DECLARE `2016 grant employee` HAS
    `in a scale of the circular's annex א'` IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed in the State's service from 1.8.2015 to 1.12.2015 continuously` IS A BOOLEAN
    `back on 2.8.2015 because 1.8.2015 was a Sabbath` IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed continuously to 2.12.2015` IS A BOOLEAN
    `his average position over 1.12.2014–30.11.2015` IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:att_3__hc_1__para_1 akn:att_3__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a akn:att_3__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a/p2 akn:att_3__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b akn:att_3__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p2
`a part of the 2016 grant for a full position` MEANS 1000

#ASSERT `a part of the 2016 grant for a full position` EQUALS `a part of the 2016 framework's one-time grant`

-- 1.ה: one paid by the hour has an auxiliary position: his monthly average
-- hours over 1.12.2014–30.11.2015 over 184.17; by the day, his monthly
-- average days over 20.83 (a five-day workplace) or 25 (six); each over the
-- time he was employed in it where he was employed in part of it.
@ref akn:att_3__hc_1__para_1__subpara_e akn:att_3__hc_1__para_1__subpara_e__cls_1 akn:att_3__hc_1__para_1__subpara_e__cls_1/p2 akn:att_3__hc_1__para_1__subpara_e__cls_2 akn:att_3__hc_1__para_1__subpara_e__cls_2/p2
GIVEN `his average monthly hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2016 grant position of one paid by the hour` `his average monthly hours` IS
    `his average monthly hours` DIVIDED BY 184.17

GIVEN `his average monthly days` IS A NUMBER, `days a week at his workplace` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2016 grant position of one paid by the day` `his average monthly days` `days a week at his workplace` IS
    IF `days a week at his workplace` EQUALS 6
    THEN `his average monthly days` DIVIDED BY 25
    ELSE `his average monthly days` DIVIDED BY 20.83

-- 1.ו with 2016-1-12 §1: an employee has the grant if he is in a scale of
-- the circular's annex א' and was employed continuously in the determining
-- period — or, by 2016-1-12, returned or started on 2.8.2015 because
-- 1.8.2015 was a Sabbath and was employed continuously to 2.12.2015; his
-- grant is in proportion to his position (1.ב).
@ref akn:att_3__hc_1__para_1__subpara_f
GIVEN e IS A `2016 grant employee`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2016 grant's first part` e IS
    IF      e's `in a scale of the circular's annex א'`
        AND (   e's `employed in the State's service from 1.8.2015 to 1.12.2015 continuously`
             OR (e's `back on 2.8.2015 because 1.8.2015 was a Sabbath` AND e's `employed continuously to 2.12.2015`))
    THEN `a part of the 2016 grant for a full position` `pro rata to a position of` (e's `his average position over 1.12.2014–30.11.2015`)
    ELSE 0

-- 1.ג: the grant is not salary for any purpose, not in severance or the
-- hour value (overtime, on-call, call-outs, duty rosters, shifts, incentive
-- pay), and carries no provident-fund contribution (training, pension or
-- managers' insurance). 1.ד: (1) not in the minimum-wage top-up; (2) it
-- does not change the combined salary table's base.
@ref akn:att_3__hc_1__para_1__subpara_c akn:att_3__hc_1__para_1__subpara_d akn:att_3__hc_1__para_1__subpara_d__cls_1 akn:att_3__hc_1__para_1__subpara_d__cls_2
`the 2016 grant is salary or carries contributions` MEANS FALSE
`the 2016 grant counts for the minimum-wage top-up` MEANS FALSE

-- 1.ו: (1) maternity leave (§6 of the Women's Work Law) in the
-- determining period does not break the continuity, and the grant is paid
-- with the first salary after the return, at the latest the next; ¶2: 26
-- weeks as a rule; (2) not unpaid leave after it, which (9) governs; (3)
-- the circular's other terms reach her; (4) so too a father on maternity
-- leave under that law. (5) reserve duty and (6) sick leave (Takshir
-- 33.210, with full, half or no pay) do not break it; (7) on sick leave
-- without pay, it is paid with the first salary on the return, at the
-- latest the next; (8) approved paid absence (rest or training leave) does
-- not break it.
DECLARE `2016 grant leave` IS ONE OF
    `maternity leave under the Women's Work Law`
    `reserve duty in the 2016 grant period`
    `sick leave under Takshir 33.210`
    `approved paid absence`
    `unpaid leave or absence treated as it`

@ref akn:att_3__hc_1__para_1__subpara_f__cls_1 akn:att_3__hc_1__para_1__subpara_f__cls_1/p2 akn:att_3__hc_1__para_1__subpara_f__cls_2 akn:att_3__hc_1__para_1__subpara_f__cls_3 akn:att_3__hc_1__para_1__subpara_f__cls_4 akn:att_3__hc_1__para_1__subpara_f__cls_5 akn:att_3__hc_1__para_1__subpara_f__cls_6 akn:att_3__hc_1__para_1__subpara_f__cls_7 akn:att_3__hc_1__para_1__subpara_f__cls_8
GIVEN k IS A `2016 grant leave`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a leave keeps the 2016 grant's continuity` k IF
    NOT k EQUALS `unpaid leave or absence treated as it`

`the maternity leave's length as a rule, in weeks, for the 2016 grant` MEANS 26

-- The Women's Work Law (imported): the 26 weeks printed are §6(ב)(1)'s
-- period for one with twelve months with the employer (the "as a rule";
-- §6(ב)(5) gives 15 to one with fewer), and keeping the period in the
-- grant's count gives at least what §6(ט) keeps — that the period harms no
-- right that turns on seniority. The floor is met; §23 keeps the rest.
`the 2016 grant's maternity leave meets the Women's Work Law` MEANS
        `the maternity leave's length as a rule, in weeks, for the 2016 grant` EQUALS `weeks of the birth and parenthood period` 12
    AND `a leave keeps the 2016 grant's continuity` `maternity leave under the Women's Work Law`
    AND `the birth and parenthood period harms no right that turns on seniority`
#ASSERT `the 2016 grant's maternity leave meets the Women's Work Law`

-- 1.ו(9): one on unpaid leave, or absence treated as it, in all or part of
-- the determining period: (1) has the grant if from 1.8.2015 to 31.1.2017
-- he had salary for 4 full months and a day at least, in a row, at any
-- position — 29.12.2016 from the signing (5.2.3.1); (2) his position is
-- his average over the part of 1.12.2014–30.11.2015 he was employed, and,
-- with no salary at all then, over 1.12.2015–30.11.2016 when he had salary
-- (in a row or not); (3) it is paid with the February 2017 salary, at the
-- latest March's — January's and February's from the signing (5.2.3.2).
@ref akn:att_3__hc_1__para_1__subpara_f__cls_9 akn:att_3__hc_1__para_1__subpara_f__cls_9__pnt_1 akn:att_3__hc_1__para_1__subpara_f__cls_9__pnt_2 akn:att_3__hc_1__para_1__subpara_f__cls_9__pnt_2/p2 akn:att_3__hc_1__para_1__subpara_f__cls_9__pnt_3
`the last day of the unpaid-leave test, as the circular prints it` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 1 2017
`the salary month an unpaid-leave grant is paid with, as the circular prints it` MEANS LIST 2017, 2

GIVEN `whole months of salary in a row` IS A NUMBER, `days more beyond them` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `one on unpaid leave has the 2016 grant` `whole months of salary in a row` `days more beyond them` IF
        `whole months of salary in a row` GREATER THAN 4
    OR (`whole months of salary in a row` EQUALS 4 AND `days more beyond them` AT LEAST 1)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the last day of the unpaid-leave test on` d IS
    IF d `is on or after` `the 2016 framework agreement was signed on`
    THEN `the last day of the unpaid-leave test, as 5.2.3 amends it`
    ELSE `the last day of the unpaid-leave test, as the circular prints it`

-- §2: the circular is agreed with the Histadrut, and the grant is part of
-- the framework agreement to be signed. §3: (א) the bodies that will sign or
-- join it and want to pay the grant to their Histadrut-scale employees are
-- approved to, by this circular; (ב) a body that pays under that approval
-- tells the wages commissioner within a month of the payment; (ג) the
-- approval is for bodies with no other agreement on pay for all of
-- 1.1.2013–31.12.2017; ¶2: one with an agreement for part of it needs the
-- wages commissioner's specific approval in advance.
@ref akn:att_3__hc_1__para_2 akn:att_3__hc_1__para_3__subpara_a akn:att_3__hc_1__para_3__subpara_b akn:att_3__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c akn:att_3__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p2
`the 2016 grant is part of the framework agreement` MEANS TRUE

GIVEN `has another agreement on pay for part of 2013–2017` IS A BOOLEAN, `has one for all of it` IS A BOOLEAN, `the wages commissioner approved it in advance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a public body may pay the 2016 grant` `has another agreement on pay for part of 2013–2017` `has one for all of it` `the wages commissioner approved it in advance` IF
        NOT `has one for all of it`
    AND ((NOT `has another agreement on pay for part of 2013–2017`) OR `the wages commissioner approved it in advance`)

`notifying the payment of the 2016 grant` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `notify the wages commissioner of paying the grant within a month`

-- The circular's annex א': the scales of the State's service the grant
-- reaches (29, a closed list — reading.closed-list); its annex ב': the two
-- it does not.
@ref akn:att_3__att_1__hc_1/p1 akn:att_3__att_1__hc_1__para_1 akn:att_3__att_1__hc_1__para_2 akn:att_3__att_1__hc_1__para_3 akn:att_3__att_1__hc_1__para_4 akn:att_3__att_1__hc_1__para_5 akn:att_3__att_1__hc_1__para_6 akn:att_3__att_1__hc_1__para_7 akn:att_3__att_1__hc_1__para_8 akn:att_3__att_1__hc_1__para_9 akn:att_3__att_1__hc_1__para_10 akn:att_3__att_1__hc_1__para_11 akn:att_3__att_1__hc_1__para_12 akn:att_3__att_1__hc_1__para_13 akn:att_3__att_1__hc_1__para_14 akn:att_3__att_1__hc_1__para_15 akn:att_3__att_1__hc_1__para_16 akn:att_3__att_1__hc_1__para_17 akn:att_3__att_1__hc_1__para_18 akn:att_3__att_1__hc_1__para_19 akn:att_3__att_1__hc_1__para_20 akn:att_3__att_1__hc_1__para_21 akn:att_3__att_1__hc_1__para_22 akn:att_3__att_1__hc_1__para_23 akn:att_3__att_1__hc_1__para_24 akn:att_3__att_1__hc_1__para_25 akn:att_3__att_1__hc_1__para_26 akn:att_3__att_1__hc_1__para_27 akn:att_3__att_1__hc_1__para_28 akn:att_3__att_1__hc_1__para_29
`the scales the 2016 grant reaches in the State's service` MEANS
    LIST "מינהלי", "אחיד", "טכנאי רנטגן", "מח\"ר, לרבות פסיכולוגים", "מהנדסים", "טכנאים והנדסאים", "פיזיותרפיסטים", "משפטנים", "סנגורים ציבוריים", "עיתונאים", "עובדי מעבדה, ביוכימאים ומיקרוביולוגים", "רוקחים", "סטודנטים לרפואה ולסיעוד", "אחים ואחיות", "פארה רפואיים", "מרפאים בעיסוק", "מפקחים ימיים", "מקצ\"ט", "סטודנטים", "מתמחים במשפטים", "נערים עובדים וחניכים", "קלדניות שופטים", "מעברי הגבול", "רשות מקרקעי ישראל", "כבאים", "עובדים סוציאליים", "שירות החוץ", "פרקליטים", "יהלום"

@ref akn:att_3__att_2__hc_1/p1 akn:att_3__att_2__hc_1__para_1 akn:att_3__att_2__hc_1__para_2
`the scales the 2016 grant does not reach in the State's service` MEANS LIST "רופאים וטרינרים", "מחקר אזרחי"

#ASSERT count `the scales the 2016 grant reaches in the State's service` EQUALS 29

