-- Circular 2016-1-12, §1: besides those of 2016-1-3's 1(א), the grant goes
-- to one who (א) was on unpaid leave (or absence treated as it, after
-- maternity leave too) and was to return on 1.8.2015, or was to start
-- then, but returned or started on 2.8.2015 because 1.8.2015 was a
-- Sabbath; (ב) was employed continuously to 2.12.2015; (ג) is on the
-- agreements of a scale of 2016-1-3's annex א' (encoded above). §2: by
-- 2016-1-3's rules, save the day of payment: §3, the February 2016
-- salary, at the latest March's; ¶5: one on sick leave without pay,
-- maternity leave or absent for an injury at work not charged to his sick
-- leave (Takshir 33.6) when it is paid has it with the first salary on his
-- return, at the latest the next. §4: one entitled under §1 has no grant
-- under 2016-1-3's 1(ו)(9): no double payment. §5: agreed with the
-- Histadrut, part of the agreement to be signed. §6: it takes nothing from
-- 2016-1-3 unless it says so.
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a__cls_1 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a__cls_2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_c akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3/p5 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_a akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_b akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c akn:att_4__hc_1__para_4 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_5 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_6
`the salary month 2016-1-12's grant is paid with` MEANS LIST 2016, 2
`the latest salary month 2016-1-12's grant is paid with` MEANS LIST 2016, 3

GIVEN `entitled under 2016-1-12` IS A BOOLEAN, `entitled under 1(ו)(9) alone` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `how many 2016 grant first parts are paid` `entitled under 2016-1-12` `entitled under 1(ו)(9) alone` IS
    IF `entitled under 2016-1-12` OR `entitled under 1(ו)(9) alone` THEN 1 ELSE 0

`a Sabbath returner` MEANS
    `2016 grant employee` WITH
        `in a scale of the circular's annex א'` IS TRUE
        `employed in the State's service from 1.8.2015 to 1.12.2015 continuously` IS FALSE
        `back on 2.8.2015 because 1.8.2015 was a Sabbath` IS TRUE
        `employed continuously to 2.12.2015` IS TRUE
        `his average position over 1.12.2014–30.11.2015` IS 0.5

#ASSERT `the 2016 grant's first part` `a Sabbath returner` EQUALS 500

-- Against the Minimum Wage Law's floor (MMS-601). §8 leaves the supplements agreed
-- within the frame, 10.6 the 2016 shekel supplement, 12.1(ד) the 2016
-- percentage supplement and the annex's 1.ד(1) the grant out of the pay
-- that counts toward the top-up: the top-up is then the law's or more (its
-- §11). §8 ¶2 counts a raise of a supplement that already counts, which §3
-- counts with it (a fixed supplement for the work, convention
-- instruments.minimum-wage-fixed-supplement): the law's own top-up. That
-- they are also an "excluded supplement" of the temporary provision of
-- תשע"ה-2015 is outside the pin (the provision has lapsed).
-- Checked on a month's figures as if §3 counted each (a fixed supplement for
-- the work), the strictest case; the law's own top-up stays owed beside them.
#ASSERT NOT `counting a component as the instrument does falls below the Minimum Wage Law` 5300 4800 (`component paid in the month under the Minimum Wage Law` `a fixed supplement paid for the work, under section 3(ב)(3)` 300) (`a 2016 framework supplement counts for the minimum-wage top-up` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `counting a component as the instrument does falls below the Minimum Wage Law` 5300 4800 (`component paid in the month under the Minimum Wage Law` `a fixed supplement paid for the work, under section 3(ב)(3)` 300) (`a 2016 framework supplement counts for the minimum-wage top-up` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `counting a component as the instrument does falls below the Minimum Wage Law` 5300 4800 (`component paid in the month under the Minimum Wage Law` `a fixed supplement paid for the work, under section 3(ב)(3)` 300) (`the 2016 shekel supplement counts for` `the 2016 framework's minimum-wage top-up`)
#ASSERT NOT `counting a component as the instrument does falls below the Minimum Wage Law` 5300 4800 (`component paid in the month under the Minimum Wage Law` `a fixed supplement paid for the work, under section 3(ב)(3)` 300) (`the framework's 2016 percentage supplement counts for` `the 2016 framework's minimum-wage top-up`)
#ASSERT NOT `counting a component as the instrument does falls below the Minimum Wage Law` 5300 4800 (`component paid in the month under the Minimum Wage Law` `a fixed supplement paid for the work, under section 3(ב)(3)` 300) (`the 2016 grant counts for the minimum-wage top-up`)

§§ `נספח ד' — דירוגים ייחודיים בשירות המדינה`

-- akn:att_5__hc_1/p1 The annex's title: the special scales of the State's service; no rule.
-- akn:att_5__hc_1__para_a/p4 The border-crossings table's title; no rule.
-- akn:att_5__hc_1__para_a/p6 The signatures; no rule.
