-- ¶2: the sections the annex serves, "(סעיפים 7.1(ג) ו-11.5-1)" —
-- F-framework-2016-d: 7.1 has no (ג); 7.2(ג) is the clause that sends the
-- special scales here, with 11.5. Read 7.2(ג) (convention reading.misprint).
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1/p2
`the clauses of 7.1` MEANS EMPTY
`the clauses of 7.2` MEANS LIST "א", "ב", "ג", "ד", "ה", "ו", "ז", "ח", "ט", "י"
`the clause annex ד' cites for the special scales` MEANS "ג"

`annex ד' cites a clause of 7.1 that 7.2 has` MEANS
        NOT elem `the clause annex ד' cites for the special scales` `the clauses of 7.1`
    AND elem `the clause annex ד' cites for the special scales` `the clauses of 7.2`

#ASSERT `annex ד' cites a clause of 7.1 that 7.2 has`

`the clause that sends the special scales to annex ד'` MEANS "7.2(ג)"

-- The annex's tables are DATA, cell for cell as the corpus publishes them:
-- a row is its label (a grade, a post) and its cells, left to right in the
-- columns' order of days. The checks below run what the agreement says of
-- them: the frame is divided in part as a uniform percentage and in part
-- as a uniform shekel sum (א ¶5), the percentage at the steps of §§12–15
-- (1.375%, 2.125%, 3%, 3.75%) and the shekel sum the 2016 shekel
-- supplement's (ב.ג, ג.ג, ד.ג).
@desc A row of one of annex ד''s tables: its label and its cells.
DECLARE `2016 special-scale row` HAS
    `the special row's label` IS A STRING
    `the special row's cells` IS A LIST OF NUMBER

-- The percentage of §§12–15 in force on each day a column of the annex
-- names, the first column being the eve.
`the percentages of the annex's columns from 1.3.2017` MEANS
    LIST 0, `the 2016 percentage supplement rate by default on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2017) EMPTY,
         `the 2016 percentage supplement rate by default on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2018) EMPTY,
         `the 2016 percentage supplement rate by default on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2018) EMPTY,
         `the 2016 percentage supplement rate by default on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2018) EMPTY

-- Each cell is its row's first cell raised by its column's percentage, to
-- the agora.
GIVEN r IS A `2016 special-scale row`, rates IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a special row keeps the percentages` r rates IF
    CONSIDER r's `the special row's cells`
    WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        all (GIVEN pair YIELD
                 CONSIDER pair
                 WHEN cell FOLLOWED BY more THEN
                     (CONSIDER more
                      WHEN rate FOLLOWED BY none THEN cell `is within an agora of` (first `increased by` rate)
                      OTHERWISE FALSE)
                 OTHERWISE FALSE)
            (zipWith (GIVEN c, k YIELD LIST c, k) (r's `the special row's cells`) rates)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- א: the border crossings. ¶2: §15 of the agreement of 2.3.2009 on the
-- scale is carried out so: ¶3 and its table, the basic salary table is
-- updated on the table's days (to 30.6.2016, from 1.7.2016, 1.3.2017,
-- 1.1.2018, 1.6.2018 and 1.12.2018). ¶5: the rise divides the whole frame
-- in part as a uniform percentage and in part as a uniform shekel sum, as
-- the parties agreed, with the special supplements' update in view (§9).
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_a akn:att_5__hc_1__para_a/p2 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_a/p3 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_a/t1 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_a/p5
`the border crossings' basic table of 2016` MEANS
    LIST `2016 special-scale row` "1" (LIST 4719, 4789.54, 4880.29, 4969.18, 5072.20, 5160.49),
         `2016 special-scale row` "2" (LIST 4903, 4973.54, 5066.81, 5157.09, 5261.72, 5351.39),
         `2016 special-scale row` "3" (LIST 5096, 5166.54, 5262.46, 5354.19, 5460.51, 5551.63),
         `2016 special-scale row` "4" (LIST 5358, 5428.54, 5528.05, 5621.76, 5730.37, 5823.46),
         `2016 special-scale row` "5" (LIST 5473, 5543.54, 5644.62, 5739.20, 5848.82, 5942.77),
         `2016 special-scale row` "6" (LIST 5663, 5733.54, 5837.23, 5933.24, 6044.52, 6139.89),
         `2016 special-scale row` "7" (LIST 5852, 5922.54, 6028.81, 6126.26, 6239.19, 6335.98),
