@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_d__subpara_b akn:att_5__hc_1__para_d__subpara_b__cls_1 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_d__subpara_b__cls_2 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_d__subpara_b__cls_3 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_d__subpara_b__cls_4 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_d__subpara_b__cls_5
`the land authority's steps` MEANS
    LIST `2016 framework step` "ד.ב.1" (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2016) (0.5%),
         `2016 framework step` "ד.ב.2" (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2017) (1.375%),
         `2016 framework step` "ד.ב.3" (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2018) (2.125%),
         `2016 framework step` "ד.ב.4" (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2018) (3%),
         `2016 framework step` "ד.ב.5" (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2018) (3.75%)

GIVEN d IS A DATE, `the employee's salary base at the authority` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a land-authority employee's rise on` d `the employee's salary base at the authority` IS
    `the employee's salary base at the authority`
    TIMES foldl (GIVEN acc, s YIELD IF d `is on or after` (s's `the step's day`) THEN s's `completed to` ELSE acc) 0 `the land authority's steps`

#ASSERT `a land-authority employee's rise on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2017) 10000 EQUALS 137.5

-- From 1.3.2017 the land authority's steps are the defaults' percentages.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN s YIELD     NOT (s's `the step's day`) `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2017)
                            OR s's `completed to` EQUALS `the 2016 percentage supplement rate by default on` (s's `the step's day`) EMPTY)
            `the land authority's steps`

-- The range table's columns from 1.3.2017: each grade's lowest and highest
-- raised by 1.37% on 1.3.2017 — F-framework-2016-a: not ד.ב(2)'s 1.375% —
-- and by ד.ב's 2.125% on 1.1.2018, to the agora; its second part by 3%
-- and 3.75% over the first part's eve. A row of the first part is the
-- grade's (lowest, highest) on the eve, 1.3.2017 and 1.1.2018 in turn.
GIVEN r IS A `2016 special-scale row`, rate2017 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a land-authority range row keeps` r rate2017 IF
    CONSIDER r's `the special row's cells`
    WHEN lo FOLLOWED BY rest1 THEN
        (CONSIDER rest1
         WHEN hi FOLLOWED BY rest2 THEN
             (CONSIDER rest2
              WHEN lo1 FOLLOWED BY rest3 THEN
                  (CONSIDER rest3
                   WHEN hi1 FOLLOWED BY rest4 THEN
                       (CONSIDER rest4
                        WHEN lo2 FOLLOWED BY rest5 THEN
                            (CONSIDER rest5
                             WHEN hi2 FOLLOWED BY none THEN
                                     lo1 `is within an agora of` (lo `increased by` rate2017)
                                 AND hi1 `is within an agora of` (hi `increased by` rate2017)
                                 AND lo2 `is within an agora of` (lo `increased by` (2.125%))
                                 AND hi2 `is within an agora of` (hi `increased by` (2.125%))
                             OTHERWISE FALSE)
                        OTHERWISE FALSE)
                   OTHERWISE FALSE)
              OTHERWISE FALSE)
         OTHERWISE FALSE)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

#ASSERT all (GIVEN r YIELD `a land-authority range row keeps` r (1.37%)) `the land authority's ranges to 1.1.2018`

`the land authority's March 2017 ranges are at 1.37%, not 1.375%` MEANS
        all (GIVEN r YIELD `a land-authority range row keeps` r (1.37%)) `the land authority's ranges to 1.1.2018`
    AND NOT any (GIVEN r YIELD `a land-authority range row keeps` r (1.375%)) `the land authority's ranges to 1.1.2018`

-- The second part: from 1.6.2018 and 1.12.2018, each grade's lowest and
-- highest at 3% and 3.75% over the eve's.
GIVEN eve IS A `2016 special-scale row`, later IS A `2016 special-scale row`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a land-authority range row of 2018 keeps` eve later IF
    CONSIDER eve's `the special row's cells`
    WHEN lo FOLLOWED BY rest1 THEN
        (CONSIDER rest1
         WHEN hi FOLLOWED BY more THEN
             (later's `the special row's cells`) `the cells are within an agora of` (LIST (lo `increased by` (3%)), (hi `increased by` (3%)), (lo `increased by` (3.75%)), (hi `increased by` (3.75%)))
         OTHERWISE FALSE)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN xs IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      ys IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE xs `the cells are within an agora of` ys IF
        count xs EQUALS count ys
    AND all (GIVEN p YIELD
                 CONSIDER p
                 WHEN x FOLLOWED BY more THEN
                     (CONSIDER more
                      WHEN y FOLLOWED BY none THEN x `is within an agora of` y
                      OTHERWISE FALSE)
                 OTHERWISE FALSE)
            (zipWith (GIVEN a, b YIELD LIST a, b) xs ys)

#ASSERT all (GIVEN p YIELD
                 CONSIDER p
                 WHEN eve FOLLOWED BY more THEN
                     (CONSIDER more
                      WHEN later FOLLOWED BY none THEN `a land-authority range row of 2018 keeps` eve later
                      OTHERWISE FALSE)
                 OTHERWISE FALSE)
            (zipWith (GIVEN a, b YIELD LIST a, b) `the land authority's ranges to 1.1.2018` `the land authority's ranges from 1.6.2018`)

@ref akn:att_5__hc_1__para_d__subpara_c akn:att_5__hc_1__para_d__subpara_c/t1 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_d__subpara_c/p3
`the land authority's 2016 shekel supplement` MEANS
    LIST `2016 special-scale row` "סכום התוספת השקלית" (LIST 70.54, 96.64, 149.90, 211.63, 264.53)

`the 2016 shekel supplement counts in the land authority's salary ceiling` MEANS TRUE

-- The three special scales have one 2016 shekel supplement, sum for sum;
-- the border crossings' table carries the same sums.
#ASSERT `the typists' 2016 shekel supplement` EQUALS `the Yahalom 2016 shekel supplement`
#ASSERT `the typists' 2016 shekel supplement` EQUALS `the land authority's 2016 shekel supplement`
#ASSERT `the cells of the special row labelled` `the typists' 2016 shekel supplement` "סכום התוספת השקלית" EQUALS `the special scales' 2016 shekel sums from 1.7.2016`

